r Defrost quickly for a gourmet meal at home pin bones pulled out Hand cut with natural variability in size (7.5-8.5 oz) Carefully wrapped in parchment paper prior to vacuum sealing. This extra step ensures the salmon never touches plastic, and provides an extra barrier that locks in premium quality. </span></p>'),(262922,76,0,117113,'<p><span>Wild Alaskan Copper River Coho are a popular salmon known for a bright color, firm texture and mild flavor. </span></p>'),(262923,85,0,117113,'Alaskan salmon, sena sea, copper river salmon'),(262924,75,0,117114,'<p><span>Wild Alaskan Copper River Coho are a popular salmon that run in August and September. Coho are know for a mild flavor and firm texture. They are bigger, fatter fish than sockeye so we cut them into larger 8oz portions, with pin-bones removed. Our Copper River Coho salmon are wild and sustainably caught out of Cordova, AK using small gillnet boats. 2020 season Copper River Coho: Known as one of the best tasting Salmon Rich reddish-orange color Medium fat, mild buttery flavor and firm texture Good source of healthy Omega 3’s (EPA and DHA) Sushi quality Wild caught, never farmed! Our 8 oz portions: Arrive individually frozen and are packed to last in your freezer for up to 1 year Defrost quickly for a gourmet meal at home pin bones pulled out Hand cut with natural variability in size (7.5-8.5 oz) Carefully wrapped in parchment paper prior to vacuum sealing. This extra step ensures the salmon never touches plastic, and provides an extra barrier that locks in premium quality. </span></p>'),(262925,76,0,117114,'<p><span>Wild Alaskan Copper River Coho are a popular salmon known for a bright color, firm texture and mild flavor. </span></p>'),(262926,85,0,117114,'Alaskan salmon, sena sea, copper river salmon'),(262927,75,0,117115,'<p><span>Wild Alaskan Copper River Coho are a popular salmon that run in August and September. Coho are know for a mild flavor and firm texture. They are bigger, fatter fish than sockeye so we cut them into larger 8oz portions, with pin-bones removed. Our Copper River Coho salmon are wild and sustainably caught out of Cordova, AK using small gillnet boats. 2020 season Copper River Coho: Known as one of the best tasting Salmon Rich reddish-orange color Medium fat, mild buttery flavor and firm texture Good source of healthy Omega 3’s (EPA and DHA) Sushi quality Wild caught, never farmed! Our 8 oz portions: Arrive individually frozen and are packed to last in your freezer for up to 1 year Defrost quickly for a gourmet meal at home pin bones pulled out Hand cut with natural variability in size (7.5-8.5 oz) Carefully wrapped in parchment paper prior to vacuum sealing. This extra step ensures the salmon never touches plastic, and provides an extra barrier that locks in premium quality. </span></p>'),(265942,75,1,117115,'<p><span>Wild Alaskan Copper River Coho are a popular salmon that run in August and September. Coho are know for a mild flavor and firm texture. They are bigger, fatter fish than sockeye so we cut them into larger 8oz portions, with pin-bones removed. Our Copper River Coho salmon are wild and sustainably caught out of Cordova, AK using small gillnet boats. 2020 season Copper River Coho: Known as one of the best tasting Salmon Rich reddish-orange color Medium fat, mild buttery flavor and firm texture Good source of healthy Omega 3’s (EPA and DHA) Sushi quality Wild caught, never farmed! Our 8 oz portions: Arrive individually frozen and are packed to last in your freezer for up to 1 year Defrost quickly for a gourmet meal at home pin bones pulled out Hand cut with natural variability in size (7.5-8.5 oz) Carefully wrapped in parchment paper prior to vacuum sealing. This extra step ensures the salmon never touches plastic, and provides an extra barrier that locks in premium quality. </span></p>'),(262928,76,0,117115,'<p><span>Wild Alaskan Copper River Coho are a popular salmon known for a bright color, firm texture and mild flavor. </span></p>'),(265943,76,1,117115,'<p><span>Wild Alaskan Copper River Coho are a popular salmon known for a bright color, firm texture and mild flavor. </span></p>'),(262929,85,0,117115,'Alaskan salmon, sena sea, copper river salmon'),(265944,85,1,117115,'Alaskan salmon, sena sea, copper river salmon'),(262930,75,0,117116,'<p><em>Classic Carmichel</em> features nearly 400 pages of hunting adventures and firearms expertise by Carmichel, widely acknowledged as one of the foremost experts on sporting arms.</p>\r\n<p>Carmichel’s exploits and prowess had no equal during what is arguably the Golden Age of international hunting and shooting. These are not just stories by a well-traveled adventurer—they are pure literature, written with a style and eloquence that deserve inclusion in any collection of great outdoor books and writers. The big 9 x 10½-inch book will feature more than a hundred never-before-published photographs.</p>'),(262932,75,1,117116,'<p><em>Classic Carmichel</em> features nearly 400 pages of hunting adventures and firearms expertise by Carmichel, widely acknowledged as one of the foremost experts on sporting arms.</p>\r\n<p>Carmichel’s exploits and prowess had no equal during what is arguably the Golden Age of international hunting and shooting. These are not just stories by a well-traveled adventurer—they are pure literature, written with a style and eloquence that deserve inclusion in any collection of great outdoor books and writers. The big 9 x 10½-inch book will feature more than a hundred never-before-published photographs.</p>'),(262931,76,0,117116,'<p>Jim Carmichel hunted around the world during his 40 years as Shooting Editor of <em>Outdoor Life</em> magazine. But none of his amazing adventures ever made it into book form —until now.</p>'),(262933,76,1,117116,'<p>Jim Carmichel hunted around the world during his 40 years as Shooting Editor of <em>Outdoor Life</em> magazine. But none of his amazing adventures ever made it into book form —until now.</p>'),(262934,85,1,117116,NULL),(262961,75,0,117130,'The BaseSlayers AMP has our Classic Carbon Alloy formula that is still firmly embedded throughout the garment to absorb odors as it always has, we\'ve just added reinforcements to increase performance and mobility. The new BaseSlayers AMP series is available in light, mid, and heavyweight styles to help you perform all season long in any season.'),(262962,75,1,117130,'The BaseSlayers AMP has our Classic Carbon Alloy formula that is still firmly embedded throughout the garment to absorb odors as it always has, we\'ve just added reinforcements to increase performance and mobility. The new BaseSlayers AMP series is available in light, mid, and heavyweight styles to help you perform all season long in any season.'),(262963,75,0,117131,'<p>Life can be likened to ascending a mountain. The higher you climb, the more years you have beneath you, the farther you can see, the more unobstructed the view, the more you understand.</p>\r\n<p><em>From A Higher Hill</em> finds Mike Gaddis atop the enlightening vantage of almost eight decades. Looking back over the vast and enthralling sporting landscape of a life well lived. And ahead, to anticipate and savor whatever years are left to come.</p>\r\n<p>Upon this lofty precipice, one of the most celebrated and insightful sporting authors of our time again reaches beyond himself, this time retrieving 65 more episodic explorations of the sporting life, the whole of which transcend contemporary perspective, and ascend to rare and unexcelled poignancy.</p>\r\n<p>Towering within a soaring cordillera of eclectic and intuitive stories and essays, every one a peak of extraordinary clarity to itself, are two pinnacle novellas, which illuminate with the force of sunlight tales of adventure heretofore bound in greater shadow. <em>Light To the Darkness, Death With the Sun</em> dawns chillingly as a life-and-death saga set deep within the spell-binding magic and mystique of the African Bushman culture, while <em>Black Widow</em> rises with blood-curdling reality to an equally riveting climax as an accompanying tale of Africa, and American hunter Dal Hardin, the man who obsessively loves her, from whom she will extract the ultimate price.</p>\r\n<p>All in all, this book stands as a colossal landmark, overlooking and broadening the expanse of sporting literature with the drama of a Kilimanjaro.</p>'),(263027,75,1,117131,'<p>Life can be likened to ascending a mountain. The higher you climb, the more years you have beneath you, the farther you can see, the more unobstructed the view, the more you understand.</p>\r\n<p><em>From A Higher Hill</em> finds Mike Gaddis atop the enlightening vantage of almost eight decades. Looking back over the vast and enthralling sporting landscape of a life well lived. And ahead, to anticipate and savor whatever years are left to come.</p>\r\n<p>Upon this lofty precipice, one of the most celebrated and insightful sporting authors of our time again reaches beyond himself, this time retrieving 65 more episodic explorations of the sporting life, the whole of which transcend contemporary perspective, and ascend to rare and unexcelled poignancy.</p>\r\n<p>Towering within a soaring cordillera of eclectic and intuitive stories and essays, every one a peak of extraordinary clarity to itself, are two pinnacle novellas, which illuminate with the force of sunlight tales of adventure heretofore bound in greater shadow. <em>Light To the Darkness, Death With the Sun</em> dawns chillingly as a life-and-death saga set deep within the spell-binding magic and mystique of the African Bushman culture, while <em>Black Widow</em> rises with blood-curdling reality to an equally riveting climax as an accompanying tale of Africa, and American hunter Dal Hardin, the man who obsessively loves her, from whom she will extract the ultimate price.</p>\r\n<p>All in all, this book stands as a colossal landmark, overlooking and broadening the expanse of sporting literature with the drama of a Kilimanjaro.</p>'),(262964,76,0,117131,'<p>One of the most celebrated and insightful sporting authors of our time again reaches beyond himself, this time retrieving 65 more episodic explorations of the sporting life.</p>'),(263028,76,1,117131,'<p>One of the most celebrated and insightful sporting authors of our time again reaches beyond himself, this time retrieving 65 more episodic explorations of the sporting life.</p>\r\n<p>Hardcover with dust jacket</p>\r\n<p>509 pages</p>'),(263029,85,1,117131,'From A Higher Hill by Mike Gaddis'),(262965,75,0,117132,'The BaseSlayers AMP has our Classic Carbon Alloy formula that is still firmly embedded throughout the garment to absorb odors as it always has, we\'ve just added reinforcements to increase performance and mobility. The new BaseSlayers AMP series is available in light, mid, and heavyweight styles to help you perform all season long in any season.'),(262966,75,1,117132,'The BaseSlayers AMP has our Classic Carbon Alloy formula that is still firmly embedded throughout the garment to absorb odors as it always has, we\'ve just added reinforcements to increase performance and mobility. The new BaseSlayers AMP series is available in light, mid, and heavyweight styles to help you perform all season long in any season.'),(262967,75,0,117133,'The BaseSlayers AMP has our Classic Carbon Alloy formula that is still firmly embedded throughout the garment to absorb odors as it always has, we\'ve just added reinforcements to increase performance and mobility. The new BaseSlayers AMP series is available in light, mid, and heavyweight styles to help you perform all season long in any season.'),(262968,75,1,117133,'The BaseSlayers AMP has our Classic Carbon Alloy formula that is still firmly embedded throughout the garment to absorb odors as it always has, we\'ve just added reinforcements to increase performance and mobility. The new BaseSlayers AMP series is available in light, mid, and heavyweight styles to help you perform all season long in any season.'),(262969,75,0,117134,'The BaseSlayers AMP has our Classic Carbon Alloy formula that is still firmly embedded throughout the garment to absorb odors as it always has, we\'ve just added reinforcements to increase performance and mobility. The new BaseSlayers AMP series is available in light, mid, and heavyweight styles to help you perform all season long in any season.'),(262970,75,1,117134,'The BaseSlayers AMP has our Classic Carbon Alloy formula that is still firmly embedded throughout the garment to absorb odors as it always has, we\'ve just added reinforcements to increase performance and mobility. The new BaseSlayers AMP series is available in light, mid, and heavyweight styles to help you perform all season long in any season.'),(262975,75,0,117139,'<p>John Banovich believes he was born to tell the lion’s story—from its ancient past to its troubling future—and in <em>King of Beasts</em>, a strikingly beautiful 12x11-inch book, he tells that story the best way he knows how—by painting Africa’s most storied predator.</p>\r\n<p>Over his illustrious 26-year career as one of the world’s foremost wildlife artists, John has continued to draw and paint the African lion more than any other subject, simply because no other animal speaks to him quite the same way.</p>\r\n<p>From LiveOak Press, <em>King of Beasts – A Study of the African Lion</em> showcases 134 stunning color plates and 20 drawings of the lion and the many fascinating creatures that share the big cat’s wild domain.</p>\r\n<p>Written by David Cabela, an expert on conservation, wildlife and things Africa, <em>King of Beasts</em> pays homage to not only to lions but also to Banovich and his remarkable achievements in art and conservation.</p>'),(345479,75,1,117139,'<p>John Banovich believes he was born to tell the lion’s story—from its ancient past to its troubling future—and in <em>King of Beasts</em>, a strikingly beautiful 12x11-inch book, he tells that story the best way he knows how—by painting Africa’s most storied predator.</p>\r\n<p>Over his illustrious 26-year career as one of the world’s foremost wildlife artists, John has continued to draw and paint the African lion more than any other subject, simply because no other animal speaks to him quite the same way.</p>\r\n<p>From LiveOak Press, <em>King of Beasts – A Study of the African Lion</em> showcases 134 stunning color plates and 20 drawings of the lion and the many fascinating creatures that share the big cat’s wild domain.</p>\r\n<p>Written by David Cabela, an expert on conservation, wildlife and things Africa, <em>King of Beasts</em> pays homage to not only to lions but also to Banovich and his remarkable achievements in art and conservation.</p>'),(262976,76,0,117139,'<p>John Banovich believes he was born to tell the lion’s story—from its ancient past to its troubling future—and in <em>King of Beasts</em>, a strikingly beautiful 12x11-inch book, he tells that story the best way he knows how—by painting Africa’s most storied predator.</p>'),(345480,76,1,117139,'<p>John Banovich believes he was born to tell the lion’s story—from its ancient past to its troubling future—and in <em>King of Beasts</em>, a strikingly beautiful 12x11-inch book, he tells that story the best way he knows how—by painting Africa’s most storied predator.</p>\r\n<p>Signed by John Banovich</p>\r\n<p>208 pages</p>'),(345481,85,1,117139,'King of Beasts: A Study of the African Lion - Collector\'s Edition - Signed by John Banovich '),(262977,75,0,117140,'<p><span>Wild Alaskan Halibut is a well-known and well-loved fish. Our Halibut is wild and sustainably caught in the gulf of Alaska by longline. Wild Alaskan Halibut: A very versatile fish with wide appeal Beautiful white meat Mild, delicate, sweet flavor with firm texture Lean meat, good source of protein Sushi quality Wild and sustainable, never farmed! Our 6oz portions: Individually vacuum sealed and frozen Defrost quickly and easily for a gourmet meal at home Hand-cut with natural variability Carefully wrapped in parchment paper prior to vacuum sealing. This extra step ensures the Salmon never touches plastic, and provides an extra oxygen barrier that locks in premium quality. </span></p>'),(262978,76,0,117140,'<p><span>Wild Alaskan Halibut are a well-known and loved fish for its pure white meat with firm texture and slightly sweet flavor. </span></p>'),(262979,85,0,117140,'Sena sea, wild alaskan halibut, halibut from alaska, fresh fish'),(262980,75,0,117141,'<p><span>Wild Alaskan Halibut is a well-known and well-loved fish. Our Halibut is wild and sustainably caught in the gulf of Alaska by longline. Wild Alaskan Halibut: A very versatile fish with wide appeal Beautiful white meat Mild, delicate, sweet flavor with firm texture Lean meat, good source of protein Sushi quality Wild and sustainable, never farmed! Our 6oz portions: Individually vacuum sealed and frozen Defrost quickly and easily for a gourmet meal at home Hand-cut with natural variability Carefully wrapped in parchment paper prior to vacuum sealing. This extra step ensures the Salmon never touches plastic, and provides an extra oxygen barrier that locks in premium quality. </span></p>'),(262981,76,0,117141,'<p><span>Wild Alaskan Halibut are a well-known and loved fish for its pure white meat with firm texture and slightly sweet flavor. </span></p>'),(262982,85,0,117141,'Sena sea, wild alaskan halibut, halibut from alaska, fresh fish'),(262983,75,0,117142,'<p><span>Wild Alaskan Halibut is a well-known and well-loved fish. Our Halibut is wild and sustainably caught in the gulf of Alaska by longline. Wild Alaskan Halibut: A very versatile fish with wide appeal Beautiful white meat Mild, delicate, sweet flavor with firm texture Lean meat, good source of protein Sushi quality Wild and sustainable, never farmed! Our 6oz portions: Individually vacuum sealed and frozen Defrost quickly and easily for a gourmet meal at home Hand-cut with natural variability Carefully wrapped in parchment paper prior to vacuum sealing. This extra step ensures the Salmon never touches plastic, and provides an extra oxygen barrier that locks in premium quality. </span></p>'),(262984,76,0,117142,'<p><span>Wild Alaskan Halibut are a well-known and loved fish for its pure white meat with firm texture and slightly sweet flavor. </span></p>'),(262985,85,0,117142,'Sena sea, wild alaskan halibut, halibut from alaska, fresh fish'),(262986,75,0,117143,'<p><span>Wild Alaskan Halibut is a well-known and well-loved fish. Our Halibut is wild and sustainably caught in the gulf of Alaska by longline. Wild Alaskan Halibut: A very versatile fish with wide appeal Beautiful white meat Mild, delicate, sweet flavor with firm texture Lean meat, good source of protein Sushi quality Wild and sustainable, never farmed! Our 6oz portions: Individually vacuum sealed and frozen Defrost quickly and easily for a gourmet meal at home Hand-cut with natural variability Carefully wrapped in parchment paper prior to vacuum sealing. This extra step ensures the Salmon never touches plastic, and provides an extra oxygen barrier that locks in premium quality. </span></p>'),(262987,76,0,117143,'<p><span>Wild Alaskan Halibut are a well-known and loved fish for its pure white meat with firm texture and slightly sweet flavor. </span></p>'),(262988,85,0,117143,'Sena sea, wild alaskan halibut, halibut from alaska, fresh fish'),(262989,75,0,117144,'<p><span>Wild Alaskan Halibut is a well-known and well-loved fish. Our Halibut is wild and sustainably caught in the gulf of Alaska by longline. Wild Alaskan Halibut: A very versatile fish with wide appeal Beautiful white meat Mild, delicate, sweet flavor with firm texture Lean meat, good source of protein Sushi quality Wild and sustainable, never farmed! Our 6oz portions: Individually vacuum sealed and frozen Defrost quickly and easily for a gourmet meal at home Hand-cut with natural variability Carefully wrapped in parchment paper prior to vacuum sealing. This extra step ensures the Salmon never touches plastic, and provides an extra oxygen barrier that locks in premium quality. </span></p>'),(359701,75,1,117144,'<p><span>Wild Alaskan Halibut is a well-known and well-loved fish. Our Halibut is wild and sustainably caught in the gulf of Alaska by longline. Wild Alaskan Halibut: A very versatile fish with wide appeal Beautiful white meat Mild, delicate, sweet flavor with firm texture Lean meat, good source of protein Sushi quality Wild and sustainable, never farmed! Our 6oz portions: Individually vacuum sealed and frozen Defrost quickly and easily for a gourmet meal at home Hand-cut with natural variability Carefully wrapped in parchment paper prior to vacuum sealing. This extra step ensures the Salmon never touches plastic, and provides an extra oxygen barrier that locks in premium quality. </span></p>'),(262990,76,0,117144,'<p><span>Wild Alaskan Halibut are a well-known and loved fish for its pure white meat with firm texture and slightly sweet flavor. </span></p>'),(359702,76,1,117144,'<p><span>Wild Alaskan Halibut are a well-known and loved fish for its pure white meat with firm texture and slightly sweet flavor. </span></p>'),(262991,85,0,117144,'Sena sea, wild alaskan halibut, halibut from alaska, fresh fish'),(359703,85,1,117144,'Sena sea, wild alaskan halibut, halibut from alaska, fresh fish'),(263017,75,0,117161,'After a long trek through the woods you stop and set up camp for the night. Imagine continuing on your journey at sunrise with yesterday\'s socks dry, fresh and soft - just as ready for the day as you are.'),(263018,75,1,117161,'After a long trek through the woods you stop and set up camp for the night. Imagine continuing on your journey at sunrise with yesterday\'s socks dry, fresh and soft - just as ready for the day as you are.'),(263025,75,0,117165,'<p>This beautiful new 240-page tabletop volume contains 189 lush black-and-white and duotone photographs, paintings and drawings that richly document the author\'s contemplative and intimately composed accounts of his hunting and fishing journeys—from Patagonia to Alaska—along with the guns, fly rods, bows and friends with whom he shared the adventures.</p>\r\n<p><span>The whisper of water on weathering stone as it courses cold around your waders, and the feel of streambed gravel beneath good felt soles. The resonant patter of rain on the brim of a trusty old hat, and the sweet, pungent aroma of November wafting through the woods on a cool autumn eve. Your first springtime walk on hillside grass following a flat, frozen interlude in hospital and rehab, and the summertime taste of fresh-picked tomatoes on your otherwise wintering tongue. A cottonwood storm in early June. </span><span>The scent of elk and horses.</span></p>\r\n<p><span><span>SUCH IS THE essence of life. </span><span>This is, after all, why we fish and hunt, and then consign the experiences to memory. </span><span>There is magic in the memories that flow from such experiences—and in the stories that result. </span><span>But no matter the spheres from where they originate, it is the memories and stories that endure, long after the last shot has been fired, the last arrow has been released, the last cast has been made, and the last trail has been trodden.</span></span></p>\r\n<p><span><span><span>Such awareness does not originate from within oneself. Instead, it is a gift from another plane, another sphere, one that is completely separate from the mundane trappings of day-to-day existence. </span><span>The hunting becomes more meaningful than the hunt, the fishing more significant than the fish. The memories become more lasting than the experiences, and the stories that result can nourish the mind and soul long after the experiences which spawned them are relegated to the past. </span><span>It is just such stories that the author shares with you here, reflecting the essence of the mountains and plains, the deserts and dunes, and the forests, waters and hemispheres from whence they come.</span></span></span></p>\r\n<p><span><span><span><strong>\"Reading a Mike Altizer story is like sitting by an evening campfire in a hunting camp. His gifts are not only those of a fine storyteller, but a conjurer of images, using words like artists\' brushes to color the landscapes of his, and our, memories.\" -Jim Carmichel</strong></span></span></span></p>\r\n<p><span><span><span><strong>\"Mike Altizer\'s poignant, sensitive style takes you to where he is and to what he\'s doing, and lets you feel what he feels. Trite as it may sound, it really is like being there yourself. The rise of a trout, the flush of a quail, the laughter of a friend and the feeling of being at the right place at sundown.\" - Steve Smith</strong></span></span></span></p>\r\n<p><span><span><span><strong>\"Mike Altizer writes good and true sentences. He stands at the top in a rare enclave of writers who are so gifted in their craft that you can\'t really put them into any sort of category.\" - Duncan Dobie</strong></span></span></span></p>'),(345482,75,1,117165,'<p>This beautiful new 240-page tabletop volume contains 189 lush black-and-white and duotone photographs, paintings and drawings that richly document the author\'s contemplative and intimately composed accounts of his hunting and fishing journeys—from Patagonia to Alaska—along with the guns, fly rods, bows and friends with whom he shared the adventures.</p>\r\n<p><span>The whisper of water on weathering stone as it courses cold around your waders, and the feel of streambed gravel beneath good felt soles. The resonant patter of rain on the brim of a trusty old hat, and the sweet, pungent aroma of November wafting through the woods on a cool autumn eve. Your first springtime walk on hillside grass following a flat, frozen interlude in hospital and rehab, and the summertime taste of fresh-picked tomatoes on your otherwise wintering tongue. A cottonwood storm in early June. </span><span>The scent of elk and horses.</span></p>\r\n<p><span><span>SUCH IS THE essence of life. </span><span>This is, after all, why we fish and hunt, and then consign the experiences to memory. </span><span>There is magic in the memories that flow from such experiences—and in the stories that result. </span><span>But no matter the spheres from where they originate, it is the memories and stories that endure, long after the last shot has been fired, the last arrow has been released, the last cast has been made, and the last trail has been trodden.</span></span></p>\r\n<p><span><span><span>Such awareness does not originate from within oneself. Instead, it is a gift from another plane, another sphere, one that is completely separate from the mundane trappings of day-to-day existence. </span><span>The hunting becomes more meaningful than the hunt, the fishing more significant than the fish. The memories become more lasting than the experiences, and the stories that result can nourish the mind and soul long after the experiences which spawned them are relegated to the past. </span><span>It is just such stories that the author shares with you here, reflecting the essence of the mountains and plains, the deserts and dunes, and the forests, waters and hemispheres from whence they come.</span></span></span></p>\r\n<p><span><span><span><strong>\"Reading a Mike Altizer story is like sitting by an evening campfire in a hunting camp. His gifts are not only those of a fine storyteller, but a conjurer of images, using words like artists\' brushes to color the landscapes of his, and our, memories.\" -Jim Carmichel</strong></span></span></span></p>\r\n<p><span><span><span><strong>\"Mike Altizer\'s poignant, sensitive style takes you to where he is and to what he\'s doing, and lets you feel what he feels. Trite as it may sound, it really is like being there yourself. The rise of a trout, the flush of a quail, the laughter of a friend and the feeling of being at the right place at sundown.\" - Steve Smith</strong></span></span></span></p>\r\n<p><span><span><span><strong>\"Mike Altizer writes good and true sentences. He stands at the top in a rare enclave of writers who are so gifted in their craft that you can\'t really put them into any sort of category.\" - Duncan Dobie</strong></span></span></span></p>'),(263026,76,0,117165,'<p>This beautiful new 240-page tabletop volume contains 189 lush black-and-white and duotone photographs, paintings and drawings that richly document the author\'s contemplative and intimately composed accounts of his hunting and fishing journeys—from Patagonia to Alaska—along with the guns, fly rods, bows and friends with whom he shared the adventures.</p>'),(345483,76,1,117165,'<p>This beautiful new 240-page tabletop volume contains 189 lush black-and-white and duotone photographs, paintings and drawings that richly document the author\'s contemplative and intimately composed accounts of his hunting and fishing journeys—from Patagonia to Alaska—along with the guns, fly rods, bows and friends with whom he shared the adventures.</p>\r\n<p>Hardcover with dust cover</p>\r\n<p>240 pages</p>'),(345484,85,1,117165,'Ramblings: Tales From Three Hemispheres -Signed by Author Michael Altizer'),(263030,75,0,117166,'After a long trek through the woods you stop and set up camp for the night. Imagine continuing on your journey at sunrise with yesterday\'s socks dry, fresh and soft - just as ready for the day as you are.'),(263031,75,1,117166,'After a long trek through the woods you stop and set up camp for the night. Imagine continuing on your journey at sunrise with yesterday\'s socks dry, fresh and soft - just as ready for the day as you are.'),(263032,75,0,117167,'After a long trek through the woods you stop and set up camp for the night. Imagine continuing on your journey at sunrise with yesterday\'s socks dry, fresh and soft - just as ready for the day as you are.'),(263033,75,1,117167,'After a long trek through the woods you stop and set up camp for the night. Imagine continuing on your journey at sunrise with yesterday\'s socks dry, fresh and soft - just as ready for the day as you are.'),(263034,75,0,117168,'After a long trek through the woods you stop and set up camp for the night. Imagine continuing on your journey at sunrise with yesterday\'s socks dry, fresh and soft - just as ready for the day as you are.'),(263035,75,1,117168,'After a long trek through the woods you stop and set up camp for the night. Imagine continuing on your journey at sunrise with yesterday\'s socks dry, fresh and soft - just as ready for the day as you are.'),(263038,75,0,117170,'After a long trek through the woods you stop and set up camp for the night. Imagine continuing on your journey at sunrise with yesterday\'s socks dry, fresh and soft - just as ready for the day as you are.'),(263039,75,1,117170,'After a long trek through the woods you stop and set up camp for the night. Imagine continuing on your journey at sunrise with yesterday\'s socks dry, fresh and soft - just as ready for the day as you are.'),(263059,75,0,117181,'<p><span>Wild Alaskan Sablefish (also called Black Cod) is found on the menus of the most exclusive seafood restaurants in the world. Our Sablefish is wild and sustainably caught in Alaska. Sablefish caught in Alaska is known to be best- with a silky texture and rich, buttery flavor. Wild Alaskan Sablefish: A favorite fish on the Japanese market Delicate, white meat High fat, rich, buttery flavor and tender, silky texture Very high in healthy Omega 3’s (EPA and DHA) Sushi quality Wild and sustainable, never farmed! Our 6oz portions: Each portion individually vacuum sealed and frozen Defrost quickly and easily for a gourmet meal at home Hand-cut with natural variability Carefully wrapped in parchment paper prior to vacuum sealing. This extra step ensures the salmon never touches plastic, and provides an extra oxygen barrier that locks in premium quality</span></p>'),(263060,76,0,117181