r working out or a casual, every day, shirt. 100% Made in USA'),(373117,75,0,174493,'This versatile T-Shirt is made from our soft, comfortable, moisture wicking, and lightweight Microtech™ fabric. Perfect for working out or a casual, every day, shirt. 100% Made in USA'),(373118,75,1,174493,'This versatile T-Shirt is made from our soft, comfortable, moisture wicking, and lightweight Microtech™ fabric. Perfect for working out or a casual, every day, shirt. 100% Made in USA'),(373119,75,0,174494,'This versatile T-Shirt is made from our soft, comfortable, moisture wicking, and lightweight Microtech™ fabric. Perfect for working out or a casual, every day, shirt. 100% Made in USA'),(373120,75,1,174494,'This versatile T-Shirt is made from our soft, comfortable, moisture wicking, and lightweight Microtech™ fabric. Perfect for working out or a casual, every day, shirt. 100% Made in USA'),(373121,75,0,174495,'This versatile T-Shirt is made from our soft, comfortable, moisture wicking, and lightweight Microtech™ fabric. Perfect for working out or a casual, every day, shirt. 100% Made in USA'),(373122,75,1,174495,'This versatile T-Shirt is made from our soft, comfortable, moisture wicking, and lightweight Microtech™ fabric. Perfect for working out or a casual, every day, shirt. 100% Made in USA'),(373124,75,0,174496,'This Sport Bra provides support with a dash of style. Two layers of comfortable and dry wicking fabric. Enhanced breathability and mobility. Comfortable straps for maximum support. 100% Made in USA'),(373214,75,1,174496,'This Sport Bra provides support with a dash of style. Two layers of comfortable and dry wicking fabric. Enhanced breathability and mobility. Comfortable straps for maximum support. 100% Made in USA'),(373125,75,0,174497,'This Sport Bra provides support with a dash of style. Two layers of comfortable and dry wicking fabric. Enhanced breathability and mobility. Comfortable straps for maximum support. 100% Made in USA'),(373215,75,1,174497,'This Sport Bra provides support with a dash of style. Two layers of comfortable and dry wicking fabric. Enhanced breathability and mobility. Comfortable straps for maximum support. 100% Made in USA'),(373126,75,0,174498,'This Sport Bra provides support with a dash of style. Two layers of comfortable and dry wicking fabric. Enhanced breathability and mobility. Comfortable straps for maximum support. 100% Made in USA'),(373216,75,1,174498,'This Sport Bra provides support with a dash of style. Two layers of comfortable and dry wicking fabric. Enhanced breathability and mobility. Comfortable straps for maximum support. 100% Made in USA'),(373127,75,0,174499,'<p>Multisport GPS Watch With Maps, Music, Metrics and More</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Premium multisport GPS smartwatch with wrist heart rate technology¹ and color TOPO maps featuring Trendline<span>™ </span>popularity routing to help you find and follow the best paths</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Fit for adventure with rugged design that features stainless steel, titanium or diamond-like carbon (DLC) titanium bezel, buttons and rear case</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Sync with music streaming services such as Spotify® to easily store and play your favorite songs right from your watch</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Garmin Pay™ contactless payment solution² lets you make convenient payments with your watch</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Built-in navigation sensors include three-axis compass, gyroscope and barometric altimeter as well as multisatellite (GPS, GLONASS and Galileo) network capability to track in more challenging environments than GPS alone</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Battery performance: up to 12 days in smartwatch mode and 8 hours in GPS mode with music (depending on settings)</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p><span>For athletes and outdoor adventurers, the fēnix 5 Plus Series watches are the high-performance way to beat yesterday and bring your maps and music along. These rugged, premium-crafted watches feature routable color mapping, wrist-based heart rate, storage for up to 1,000 songs and our </span>Garmin Pay<span> contactless payment solution.</span></p>\r\n<p>Your Roadmap to Success</p>\r\n<p>Whether you’re in the city or on the trail, all fēnix 5 Plus Series watches provide built-in mapping and navigation features to help keep you oriented and on course. Full-color TOPO mapping comes preloaded with map data optimized for at-a-glance navigation and location tracking. For runners and cyclists, the device also features Trendline popularity routing, which uses billions of miles of Garmin Connect<span>™ </span>data to help you find and follow the best trails and routes.</p>\r\n<p>Multinetwork Navigation</p>\r\n<p>Every fēnix 5 Plus Series watch features multinetwork (GPS, GLONASS and Galileo) satellite reception to track in more challenging environments than GPS alone. In addition to map-based guidance, each watch also provides a set of ABC (altimeter, barometer and compass) sensors for outdoor navigation. The built-in altimeter provides elevation data to accurately monitor ascent and descent for activities such as hiking, while the tilt-compensated three-axis electronic compass keeps your bearing — whether you’re moving or not.</p>\r\n<p>Advanced Performance Metrics</p>\r\n<p>When you’re pushing your limits, you need a decisive edge. fēnix delivers with sophisticated training features to monitor your form and performance. Tap into physiological metrics, running dynamics and more to track your workout stats, measure your progress and fine-tune your form. Training status automatically evaluates your recent exercise history and performance indicators to let you know if you’re overtraining, maintaining or peaking. You can also view your overall training load, which measures your exercise volume from the last 7 days and compares it to the optimal range for your fitness and recent training history. Special preloaded activity profiles are provided for swimming, running, biking, hiking, skiing, rowing, paddle boarding and more. For added motivation, download advanced workouts and training plans from Garmin Connect.</p>\r\n<p>Wrist-based Heart Rate</p>\r\n<p>On your wrist, Elevate<span>™</span> wrist heart rate technology lets you monitor your heart rate without wearing a chest strap. In addition to counting steps and monitoring sleep, the watch uses heart rate to provide calories burned information and quantify the intensity of your fitness activities. It also measures your heart rate variability to calculate a stress score that helps you assess what level of activity your body is ready for.</p>\r\n<p>A Little Traveling Music</p>\r\n<p>Got a power song that gets you pumped up for a race or tough workout? Now you can have up to 1,000 songs stored right on your watch, for phone-free listening on the go. It’s easy to transfer music from your computer and then queue up your favorite playlist for easy listening through compatible Bluetooth headphones (sold separately). fēnix 5 Plus Series is also compatible with some of your favorite streaming services — and more are being added all the time. </p>\r\n<p>Pay with a Wave of Your Hand</p>\r\n<p>To help keep pace with your active lifestyle, fēnix 5 Plus devices feature our Garmin Pay contactless payment solution. Use it to pay for purchases so you can breeze through checkout lines while leaving your cash and cards at home. It works just about anywhere there’s a scanner for contactless payments.</p>\r\n<p>Safety and Tracking Features</p>\r\n<p>fēnix 5 Plus provides safety and tracking features<span>4</span> to help provide a little extra peace of mind for you and your loved ones. If anything should happen — and your watch is paired with your compatible smartphone — hold the light button down until you feel the watch vibrate 3 times. This activates the assistance feature, which discreetly sends a message with your real-time location to your preloaded emergency contacts. That way, help has an easier time finding you. This watch also has incident detection, which automatically sends a message with your real-time location to preloaded emergency contacts if an incident is detected during an outdoor walk, run, hike or bike activity.<span></span></p>\r\n<p>Premium Materials, Robust Performance</p>\r\n<p>Built for rugged adventures and crafted of the finest premium-grade materials, fēnix 5 Plus Series watches are available in a variety of finish choices, including PVD-coated stainless steel bezel and DLC titanium bezel version. A bright, high-resolution, full-color Garmin Chroma Display™ with LED backlighting assures readability in all ambient conditions. And transflective technology that reflects and transmits light at the same time enables the watch face to become even more readable under intense sunlight. For added scratch resistance, a high-strength domed sapphire lens is available on several fēnix 5 Plus Series models.</p>\r\n<p>Custom Apps, Watch Faces and Bands</p>\r\n<p>You can customize any fēnix watch with free downloads from our Connect IQ™ store. Change your watch face, add data fields or get apps and widgets for information at a glance. There’s also a wide selection of QuickFit<span>®</span> bands in your choice of premium leather, metal or silicone — so it’s easy to mix and match styles to go with any sport or activity. No tools are required to make the transformation. Just swap, click and go. With Garmin, you can add personality to your watch that’s uniquely you.</p>\r\n<p></p>\r\n<p>Running Power</p>\r\n<p>Add power data to your training by downloading our Running Power app from the Connect IQ store onto your compatible watch. Developed by Garmin Labs, the Running Power app taps into metrics — such as pace, vertical oscillation, grade and even local wind conditions — to determine the amount of power you’re applying at the ground as you run. When you know how much power you’re expending from minute to minute and mile to mile, you’re better able to pace yourself, which can help keep you from tiring out too quickly. The best news? If you already own the right Garmin devices, adding power to your run is free. </p>'),(373136,75,1,174499,'<p>Multisport GPS Watch With Maps, Music, Metrics and More</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Premium multisport GPS smartwatch with wrist heart rate technology¹ and color TOPO maps featuring Trendline<span>™ </span>popularity routing to help you find and follow the best paths</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Fit for adventure with rugged design that features stainless steel, titanium or diamond-like carbon (DLC) titanium bezel, buttons and rear case</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Sync with music streaming services such as Spotify® to easily store and play your favorite songs right from your watch</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Garmin Pay™ contactless payment solution² lets you make convenient payments with your watch</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Built-in navigation sensors include three-axis compass, gyroscope and barometric altimeter as well as multisatellite (GPS, GLONASS and Galileo) network capability to track in more challenging environments than GPS alone</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Battery performance: up to 12 days in smartwatch mode and 8 hours in GPS mode with music (depending on settings)</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p><span>For athletes and outdoor adventurers, the fēnix 5 Plus Series watches are the high-performance way to beat yesterday and bring your maps and music along. These rugged, premium-crafted watches feature routable color mapping, wrist-based heart rate, storage for up to 1,000 songs and our </span>Garmin Pay<span> contactless payment solution.</span></p>\r\n<p>Your Roadmap to Success</p>\r\n<p>Whether you’re in the city or on the trail, all fēnix 5 Plus Series watches provide built-in mapping and navigation features to help keep you oriented and on course. Full-color TOPO mapping comes preloaded with map data optimized for at-a-glance navigation and location tracking. For runners and cyclists, the device also features Trendline popularity routing, which uses billions of miles of Garmin Connect<span>™ </span>data to help you find and follow the best trails and routes.</p>\r\n<p>Multinetwork Navigation</p>\r\n<p>Every fēnix 5 Plus Series watch features multinetwork (GPS, GLONASS and Galileo) satellite reception to track in more challenging environments than GPS alone. In addition to map-based guidance, each watch also provides a set of ABC (altimeter, barometer and compass) sensors for outdoor navigation. The built-in altimeter provides elevation data to accurately monitor ascent and descent for activities such as hiking, while the tilt-compensated three-axis electronic compass keeps your bearing — whether you’re moving or not.</p>\r\n<p>Advanced Performance Metrics</p>\r\n<p>When you’re pushing your limits, you need a decisive edge. fēnix delivers with sophisticated training features to monitor your form and performance. Tap into physiological metrics, running dynamics and more to track your workout stats, measure your progress and fine-tune your form. Training status automatically evaluates your recent exercise history and performance indicators to let you know if you’re overtraining, maintaining or peaking. You can also view your overall training load, which measures your exercise volume from the last 7 days and compares it to the optimal range for your fitness and recent training history. Special preloaded activity profiles are provided for swimming, running, biking, hiking, skiing, rowing, paddle boarding and more. For added motivation, download advanced workouts and training plans from Garmin Connect.</p>\r\n<p>Wrist-based Heart Rate</p>\r\n<p>On your wrist, Elevate<span>™</span> wrist heart rate technology lets you monitor your heart rate without wearing a chest strap. In addition to counting steps and monitoring sleep, the watch uses heart rate to provide calories burned information and quantify the intensity of your fitness activities. It also measures your heart rate variability to calculate a stress score that helps you assess what level of activity your body is ready for.</p>\r\n<p>A Little Traveling Music</p>\r\n<p>Got a power song that gets you pumped up for a race or tough workout? Now you can have up to 1,000 songs stored right on your watch, for phone-free listening on the go. It’s easy to transfer music from your computer and then queue up your favorite playlist for easy listening through compatible Bluetooth headphones (sold separately). fēnix 5 Plus Series is also compatible with some of your favorite streaming services — and more are being added all the time. </p>\r\n<p>Pay with a Wave of Your Hand</p>\r\n<p>To help keep pace with your active lifestyle, fēnix 5 Plus devices feature our Garmin Pay contactless payment solution. Use it to pay for purchases so you can breeze through checkout lines while leaving your cash and cards at home. It works just about anywhere there’s a scanner for contactless payments.</p>\r\n<p>Safety and Tracking Features</p>\r\n<p>fēnix 5 Plus provides safety and tracking features<span>4</span> to help provide a little extra peace of mind for you and your loved ones. If anything should happen — and your watch is paired with your compatible smartphone — hold the light button down until you feel the watch vibrate 3 times. This activates the assistance feature, which discreetly sends a message with your real-time location to your preloaded emergency contacts. That way, help has an easier time finding you. This watch also has incident detection, which automatically sends a message with your real-time location to preloaded emergency contacts if an incident is detected during an outdoor walk, run, hike or bike activity.<span></span></p>\r\n<p>Premium Materials, Robust Performance</p>\r\n<p>Built for rugged adventures and crafted of the finest premium-grade materials, fēnix 5 Plus Series watches are available in a variety of finish choices, including PVD-coated stainless steel bezel and DLC titanium bezel version. A bright, high-resolution, full-color Garmin Chroma Display™ with LED backlighting assures readability in all ambient conditions. And transflective technology that reflects and transmits light at the same time enables the watch face to become even more readable under intense sunlight. For added scratch resistance, a high-strength domed sapphire lens is available on several fēnix 5 Plus Series models.</p>\r\n<p>Custom Apps, Watch Faces and Bands</p>\r\n<p>You can customize any fēnix watch with free downloads from our Connect IQ™ store. Change your watch face, add data fields or get apps and widgets for information at a glance. There’s also a wide selection of QuickFit<span>®</span> bands in your choice of premium leather, metal or silicone — so it’s easy to mix and match styles to go with any sport or activity. No tools are required to make the transformation. Just swap, click and go. With Garmin, you can add personality to your watch that’s uniquely you.</p>\r\n<p></p>\r\n<p>Running Power</p>\r\n<p>Add power data to your training by downloading our Running Power app from the Connect IQ store onto your compatible watch. Developed by Garmin Labs, the Running Power app taps into metrics — such as pace, vertical oscillation, grade and even local wind conditions — to determine the amount of power you’re applying at the ground as you run. When you know how much power you’re expending from minute to minute and mile to mile, you’re better able to pace yourself, which can help keep you from tiring out too quickly. The best news? If you already own the right Garmin devices, adding power to your run is free. </p>'),(373128,76,0,174499,'<p id=\"js__product__info__variation\" class=\"app__product__info__subtitle\">Sapphire, Black with Black Band</p>\r\n<p class=\"app__product__info__subtitle\">47mm case size</p>'),(373137,76,1,174499,'<p id=\"js__product__info__variation\" class=\"app__product__info__subtitle\">Sapphire, Black with Black Band</p>\r\n<p class=\"app__product__info__subtitle\">47mm case size</p>\r\n<p class=\"app__product__info__subtitle\">10 ATM</p>\r\n<p class=\"app__product__info__subtitle\">16gb Memory</p>\r\n<p class=\"app__product__info__subtitle\">Battery Life:</p>\r\n<p class=\"app__product__info__subtitle\"><span>Smartwatch: Up to 12 days</span><br /><span>GPS: Up to 18 hours</span><br /><span>GPS and Music: Up to 8 hours</span><br /><span>UltraTrac™ mode: Up to 42 hours</span></p>'),(373129,85,0,174499,'Garmin fēnix® 5 Plus'),(373138,85,1,174499,'Garmin fēnix® 5 Plus'),(373130,75,0,174500,'<h2 class=\"app__overview__intro__title light center\" data-v-5b9e0d04=\"\" data-test=\"gc__heading\">WHEN YOU CAN RELY ON INSTINCT, THE WORLD CAN RELY ON YOU!</h2>\r\n<div class=\"app__overview__intro__description gc__copy gc__copy--light gc__copy--center gc__copy--large\" data-v-f2ba670e=\"\" data-test=\"gc__copy\">\r\n<p>You’ve never been one to follow the beaten path — that’s where Instinct comes in. This rugged GPS watch was built to withstand the toughest environments.</p>\r\n<p><span>Withstand the elements with military standard toughness.</span></p>\r\n<span>Navigate your world with multi-GNSS satellite support and outdoor sensors.</span></div>\r\n<div class=\"app__overview__intro__description gc__copy gc__copy--light gc__copy--center gc__copy--large\" data-v-f2ba670e=\"\" data-test=\"gc__copy\">\r\n<p><span></span></p>\r\n<p><span>Train smarter with built-in sports app right on your wrist.</span></p>\r\n<p><span>Pair with your compatible smartphone for on-wrist messaging, alerts and notifications.</span></p>\r\n<p><span>Map, track, sync and share your trek from anywhere with our exclusive app.</span></p>\r\n<p><span>Don\'t be limited by battery life. Get up to 14 days in smartwatch mode.</span></p>\r\n</div>'),(373133,75,1,174500,'<h2 class=\"app__overview__intro__title light center\" data-v-5b9e0d04=\"\" data-test=\"gc__heading\">WHEN YOU CAN RELY ON INSTINCT, THE WORLD CAN RELY ON YOU!</h2>\r\n<div class=\"app__overview__intro__description gc__copy gc__copy--light gc__copy--center gc__copy--large\" data-v-f2ba670e=\"\" data-test=\"gc__copy\">\r\n<p>You’ve never been one to follow the beaten path — that’s where Instinct comes in. This rugged GPS watch was built to withstand the toughest environments.</p>\r\n<p><span>Withstand the elements with military standard toughness.</span></p>\r\n<span>Navigate your world with multi-GNSS satellite support and outdoor sensors.</span></div>\r\n<div class=\"app__overview__intro__description gc__copy gc__copy--light gc__copy--center gc__copy--large\" data-v-f2ba670e=\"\" data-test=\"gc__copy\">\r\n<p><span></span></p>\r\n<p><span>Train smarter with built-in sports app right on your wrist.</span></p>\r\n<p><span>Pair with your compatible smartphone for on-wrist messaging, alerts and notifications.</span></p>\r\n<p><span>Map, track, sync and share your trek from anywhere with our exclusive app.</span></p>\r\n<p><span>Don\'t be limited by battery life. Get up to 14 days in smartwatch mode.</span></p>\r\n</div>'),(373131,76,0,174500,'<p id=\"js__product__info__variation\" class=\"app__product__info__subtitle\">Graphite</p>\r\n<p class=\"app__product__info__subtitle\">10ATM</p>\r\n<p class=\"app__product__info__subtitle\">16 mb memory</p>\r\n<p class=\"app__product__info__subtitle\">Battery life:</p>\r\n<p class=\"app__product__info__subtitle\"><span>Smartwatch mode: Up to 14 days</span><br /><span>GPS mode: Up to 16 hours</span><br /><span>UltraTrac™ mode: Up to 40 hours</span></p>'),(373134,76,1,174500,'<p id=\"js__product__info__variation\" class=\"app__product__info__subtitle\">Graphite</p>\r\n<p class=\"app__product__info__subtitle\">10ATM</p>\r\n<p class=\"app__product__info__subtitle\">16 mb memory</p>\r\n<p class=\"app__product__info__subtitle\">Battery life:</p>\r\n<p class=\"app__product__info__subtitle\"><span>Smartwatch mode: Up to 14 days</span><br /><span>GPS mode: Up to 16 hours</span><br /><span>UltraTrac™ mode: Up to 40 hours</span></p>'),(373132,85,0,174500,'Garmin Instinct® Graphite Watch, instinct watch, garmin watch'),(373135,85,1,174500,'Garmin Instinct® Graphite Watch, instinct watch, garmin watch'),(373139,75,0,174501,'<p>Explore the World with Reliable Navigation in Hand</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Rugged and water-resistant design with button operation and a 2.6” sunlight-readable color display</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Preloaded with TopoActive maps, featuring routable roads and trails for cycling and hiking</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Know where you’re at with a high-sensitivity receiver with quad helix antenna and multi-GNSS support (GPS, GLONASS and Galileo) and 3-axis compass with barometric altimeter</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Battery life: up to 16 hours in GPS mode</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>Navigate your next adventure with the GPSMAP 64x handheld navigator series. Whether you’re hiking, cycling, geocaching or climbing, you are free to explore more with proven Garmin handheld navigation in the palm of your hand. And the series now has multi-GNSS support and TopoActive mapping.   </p>\r\n<div class=\"row top-m bottom-m\">\r\n<div class=\"span12\">\r\n<p>Explore the Terrain</p>\r\n<p>The GPSMAP 64x handheld series comes preloaded with TopoActive maps featuring routable streets and trails so you can take the journey off the grid. Now you can know your surroundings — such as waterways and natural features as well as buildings, international boundaries and more. You can also find thousands of points of interests, including shops, restaurants, universities, parks and accommodations.</p>\r\n<p>Keep Your Fix</p>\r\n<p>With its quad helix antenna and high-sensitivity receiver and multiple global navigation system support (GPS, GLONASS and Galileo), the GPSMAP 64x series locates your position quickly and precisely and maintains its location in more challenging environments than GPS alone.</p>\r\n<p>Satellite Imagery</p>\r\n<p>The GPSMAP 64x series also supports BirdsEye Satellite Imagery (subscription required) that lets you load satellite images and integrate them with your maps.</p>\r\n<p>Document Your Journey</p>\r\n<p>With GPSMAP 64csx, you can capture the highlights of your outings with the built-in 8-megapixel autofocus camera. Each photo is automatically geotagged with the location of where it was taken, allowing you — or those you share your photos with — to easily navigate back to that spot in the future.</p>\r\n<p>Find Fun</p>\r\n<p>The GPSMAP 64x series features paperless geocaching. Upload GPX files straight to your device, and view key information such as location, terrain and hints from Geocaching.com.</p>\r\n<p></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>'),(373333,75,1,174501,'<p>Explore the World with Reliable Navigation in Hand</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Rugged and water-resistant design with button operation and a 2.6” sunlight-readable color display</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Preloaded with TopoActive maps, featuring routable roads and trails for cycling and hiking</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Know where you’re at with a high-sensitivity receiver with quad helix antenna and multi-GNSS support (GPS, GLONASS and Galileo) and 3-axis compass with barometric altimeter</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Battery life: up to 16 hours in GPS mode</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>Navigate your next adventure with the GPSMAP 64x handheld navigator series. Whether you’re hiking, cycling, geocaching or climbing, you are free to explore more with proven Garmin handheld navigation in the palm of your hand. And the series now has multi-GNSS support and TopoActive mapping.   </p>\r\n<div class=\"row top-m bottom-m\">\r\n<div class=\"span12\">\r\n<p>Explore the Terrain</p>\r\n<p>The GPSMAP 64x handheld series comes preloaded with TopoActive maps featuring routable streets and trails so you can take the journey off the grid. Now you can know your surroundings — such as waterways and natural features as well as buildings, international boundaries and more. You can also find thousands of points of interests, including shops, restaurants, universities, parks and accommodations.</p>\r\n<p>Keep Your Fix</p>\r\n<p>With its quad helix antenna and high-sensitivity receiver and multiple global navigation system support (GPS, GLONASS and Galileo), the GPSMAP 64x series locates your position quickly and precisely and maintains its location in more challenging environments than GPS alone.</p>\r\n<p>Satellite Imagery</p>\r\n<p>The GPSMAP 64x series also supports BirdsEye Satellite Imagery (subscription required) that lets you load satellite images and integrate them with your maps.</p>\r\n<p>Document Your Journey</p>\r\n<p>With GPSMAP 64csx, you can capture the highlights of your outings with the built-in 8-megapixel autofocus camera. Each photo is automatically geotagged with the location of where it was taken, allowing you — or those you share your photos with — to easily navigate back to that spot in the future.</p>\r\n<p>Find Fun</p>\r\n<p>The GPSMAP 64x series features paperless geocaching. Upload GPX files straight to your device, and view key information such as location, terrain and hints from Geocaching.com.</p>\r\n<p></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>'),(373140,76,0,174501,'<p>PHYSICAL DIMENSIONS: 2.4\" x 6.3\" x 1.4\" (6.1 x 16.0 x 3.6 cm)<br />DISPLAY SIZE: 1.43\" x 2.15\" (3.6 x 5.5 cm); 2.6\" diag (6.6 cm)<br />DISPLAY RESOLUTION: 160 x 240 pixels<br />DISPLAY TYPE: transflective, 65K color TFT<br />WEIGHT: 7.7 oz (217 g) with batteries</p>'),(373334,76,1,174501,'<p>PHYSICAL DIMENSIONS: 2.4\" x 6.3\" x 1.4\" (6.1 x 16.0 x 3.6 cm)<br />DISPLAY SIZE: 1.43\" x 2.15\" (3.6 x 5.5 cm); 2.6\" diag (6.6 cm)<br />DISPLAY RESOLUTION: 160 x 240 pixels<br />DISPLAY TYPE: transflective, 65K color TFT<br />WEIGHT: 7.7 oz (217 g) with batteries</p>'),(373141,85,0,174501,'Garmin GPSMAP® 64x Handheld GPS, gps, garmin gps, garmin handheld, handheld gps, everest.com'),(373335,85,1,174501,'Garmin GPSMAP® 64x Handheld GPS, gps, garmin gps, garmin handheld, handheld gps, everest.com'),(373146,75,0,174502,'<p>The X-Vision Optics XANB25 Deluxe Digital Night Vision Binoculars bring together affordability, functionality and capability all into one device. From its recording and picture taking abilities to its lightweight user-friendly design, this unit was built to show off the night and every other aspect of the world that demands to be seen from afar. Package comes with a padded neck strap for support on any type of adventure.</p>\r\n<h5><span>HIGH PERFORMANCE DISTANCE RANGE.</span></h5>\r\n<p>See as far as 150 yards (137 m) in complete darkness, or up to 400 yards (366 m) during the day. Field of view at 100 yards (91 m) is 20 yards (18 m) to ensure nothing ever goes unnoticed. This binocular is perfect for hunting, camping, sports, wildlife observation, farm monitoring, sightseeing, etc. Discover The Unseen.</p>\r\n<h5><span>HIGH QUALITY MATERIALS AND ERGONOMIC DESIGN.</span></h5>\r\n<p>Dust and water resistant to an International Protection Rating of IP52. Weighs 1.54 pounds (0.70 kg) for optimal comfort. This X-Vision Optics Night Vision Digital Binocular is perfect for any harsh environment with its heavy-duty exterior that is durable and built to last. Package comes with a padded neck strap for support during all types of adventure.</p>\r\n<h5><span>LONG BATTERY LIFE FOR BOTH DAY AND NIGHT USE.</span></h5>\r\n<p>Battery life consists of long continuous use with 10 hours of performance in the daytime or 6 hours of performance at nighttime. This X-Vision binocular operates on 8 AA batteries (sold separately).</p>\r\n<h5><span>REMEMBER THE ADVENTURE WITH PHOTO AND VIDEO CAPABILITY.</span></h5>\r\n<p>Take your goggles into the dark of night and clearly capture objects in total darkness on a large viewing screen. Zoom in up to 2x. This night vision goggle has the ability to record video and take pictures with up to a 32 GB micro SD card (sold separately) to transfer onto your computer for later viewing.</p>\r\n<h5><span>EASY TO USE FOR BOTH BEGINNERS AND PROFESSIONALS.</span></h5>\r\n<p>5 simple buttons for straightforward operation. The focus dial on the bottom of the digital night vision binoculars adjusts the view so you can manually focus on any animal or object around you. Can comfortably view with both eyes, including the use of glasses.</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Viewfinder: EVF mode</li>\r\n<li>Aspect ratio: 4:3</li>\r\n<li>Aperture: F1.4 with adjustable aperture day and night dual mode Operation: Preview / photo play back</li>\r\n<li>Night Time Full Dark Distance: 150 yards</li>\r\n<li>Day Time Max Distance: 400 yards</li>\r\n<li>Optical Lens: 3x</li>\r\n<li>Minimum Zoom: 3x</li>\r\n<li>Maximum Zoom: 6x</li>\r\n<li>Field of View @ 100 yards: 20 yards</li>\r\n<li>Photo capability: Yes</li>\r\n<li>Video Capability: Yes</li>\r\n<li>Object lens focus: Manually adjustable</li>\r\n<li>Visual angle: 10 degrees</li>\r\n<li>Luminance: IR LED / total 2W</li>\r\n<li>External Memory: Up to 32GB SD card</li>\r\n<li>Battery Type: AA</li>\r\n<li>Battery Quantity: 8</li>\r\n<li>Rechargeable: No</li>\r\n<li>Day Time Battery Life: 10 hours</li>\r\n<li>Night Time Battery Life: 6 hours</li>\r\n<li>Power consumption: 2.5W with IR LED fully on</li>\r\n<li>Unit Size: 7.28in x 5.70in x 2.16in / 18.50cm x 14.47cm x 5.48cm (approx.)</li>\r\n<li>Weight: 1.33 pounds / 0.60 kg (approx.)</li>\r\n</ul>'),(675705,75,1,174502,'<p>The X-Vision Optics XANB25 Deluxe Digital Night Vision Binoculars bring together affordability, functionality and capability all into one device. From its recording and picture taking abilities to its lightweight user-friendly design, this unit was built to show off the night and every other aspect of the world that demands to be seen from afar. Package comes with a padded neck strap for support on any type of adventure.</p>\r\n<h5><span>HIGH PERFORMANCE DISTANCE RANGE.</span></h5>\r\n<p>See as far as 150 yards (137 m) in complete darkness, or up to 400 yards (366 m) during the day. Field of view at 100 yards (91 m) is 20 yards (18 m) to ensure nothing ever goes unnoticed. This binocular is perfect for hunting, camping, sports, wildlife observation, farm monitoring, sightseeing, etc. Discover The Unseen.</p>\r\n<h5><span>HIGH QUALITY MATERIALS AND ERGONOMIC DESIGN.</span></h5>\r\n<p>Dust and water resistant to an International Protection Rating of IP52. Weighs 1.54 pounds (0.70 kg) for optimal comfort. This X-Vision Optics Night Vision Digital Binocular is perfect for any harsh environment with its heavy-duty exterior that is durable and built to last. Package comes with a padded neck strap for support during all types of adventure.</p>\r\n<h5><span>LONG BATTERY LIFE FOR BOTH DAY AND NIGHT USE.</span></h5>\r\n<p>Battery life consists of long continuous use with 10 hours of performance in the daytime or 6 hours of performance at nighttime. This X-Vision binocular operates on 8 AA batteries (sold separately).</p>\r\n<h5><span>REMEMBER THE ADVENTURE WITH PHOTO AND VIDEO CAPABILITY.</span></h5>\r\n<p>Take your goggles into the dark of night and clearly capture objects in total darkness on a large viewing screen. Zoom in up to 2x. This night vision goggle has the ability to record video and take pictures with up to a 32 GB micro SD card (sold separately) to transfer onto your computer for later viewing.</p>\r\n<h5><span>EASY TO USE FOR BOTH BEGINNERS AND PROFESSIONALS.</span></h5>\r\n<p>5 simple buttons for straightforward operation. The focus dial on the bottom of the digital night vision binoculars adjusts the view so you can manually focus on any animal or object around you. Can comfortably view with both eyes, including the use of glasses.</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Viewfinder: EVF mode</li>\r\n<li>Aspect ratio: 4:3</li>\r\n<li>Aperture: F1.4 with adjustable aperture day and night dual mode Operation: Preview / photo play back</li>\r\n<li>Night Time Full Dark Distance: 150 yards</li>\r\n<li>Day Time Max Distance: 400 yards</li>\r\n<li>Optical Lens: 3x</li>\r\n<li>Minimum Zoom: 3x</li>\r\n<li>Maximum Zoom: 6x</li>\r\n<li>Field of View @ 100 yards: 20 yards</li>\r\n<li>Photo capability: Yes</li>\r\n<li>Video Capability: Yes</li>\r\n<li>Object lens focus: Manually adjustable</li>\r\n<li>Visual angle: 10 degrees</li>\r\n<li>Luminance: IR LED / total 2W</li>\r\n<li>External Memory: Up to 32GB SD card</li>\r\n<li>Battery Type: AA</li>\r\n<li>Battery Quantity: 8</li>\r\n<li>Rechargeable: No</li>\r\n<li>Day Time Battery Life: 10 hours</li>\r\n<li>Night Time Battery Life: 6 hours</li>\r\n<li>Power consumption: 2.5W with IR LED fully on</li>\r\n<li>Unit Size: 7.28in x 5.70in x 2.16in / 18.50cm x 14.47cm x 5.48cm (approx.)</li>\r\n<li>Weight: 1.33 pounds / 0.60 kg (approx.)</li>\r\n</ul>'),(373147,76,0,174502,'<p>The X-Vision Optics XANB25 Deluxe Digital Night Vision Binoculars bring together affordability, functionality and capability all into one device. From its recording and picture taking abilities to its lightweight user-friendly design, this unit was built to show off the night and every other aspect of the world that demands to be seen from afar. Package comes with a padded neck strap for support on any type of adventure.</p>'),(675707,76,1,174502,'<p>The X-Vision Optics XANB25 Deluxe Digital Night Vision Binoculars bring together affordability, functionality and capability all into one device. From its recording and picture taking abilities to its lightweight user-friendly design, this unit was built to show off the night and every other aspect of the world that demands to be seen from afar. Package comes with a padded neck strap for support on any type of adventure.</p>'),(373148,85,0,174502,'X-Vision Digital Night Vision Binoculars Model #XANB25'),(675706,85,1,174502,'X-Vision Digital Night Vision Binoculars Model #XANB25'),(373149,75,0,174503,'<p><span><span>The Annie Oakley Silver Dollar</span></span></p>\r\n<p>“Little Miss Sure Shot” Annie Oakley may have been only five feet tall, but she was also arguably the deadliest woman of her day with a rifle! Thanks to her incredible marksmanship, Annie joined Buffalo Bill’s touring show in 1885, becoming America’s first female star, performing for royalty across Europe, and earning more than anyone in the company besides Buffalo Bill himself! In 1898, the year this Morgan Silver Dollar was struck, Annie promoted the service of women in combat, going so far as to offer President McKinley the service of 50 female sharpshooters should the U.S. go to war with Spain. The offer wasn’t accepted, but you can still take home this Brilliant Uncirculated (BU) Morgan Silver Dollar struck at the “Mother Mint” in Philadelphia that same year, housed in a custom card featuring Annie Oakley.</p>\r\n<p><span><span>COIN HIGHLIGHTS:</span></span></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li><span>AMERICA’S MOST POPULAR COIN –</span> The Morgan Silver Dollar – so named for its designer, U.S. Mint Assistant Engraver George T. Morgan — has stood the test of time. Struck from 1878-1904 and again in 1921, it was the coin of America’s “Wild West” and jingled in the coin purses of gamblers, gunfighters, soldiers and dance hall girls.</li>\r\n<li><span>CLASSIC DESIGNS –</span> Morgan’s historic design depicts a profile of Lady Liberty on the obverse while the reverse features an eagle with outstretched wings. The model used for Liberty was Miss Anna Williams of Philadelphia, who Morgan declared to have the most perfect feminine profile he had ever seen.</li>\r\n<li><span>STRUCK IN GLEAMING AMERICAN SILVER –</span> Struck in 26.73 grams of 90% silver from the famous Comstock Lode, the Morgan Silver Dollar is a big coin 38.1 mm in diameter. When this coin was plunked down on a counter, its weight meant real money, pure and simple.</li>\r\n<li><span>LEGAL TENDER SILVER DOLLAR –</span> Morgans were $1 legal tender and struck during the heyday of America’s Wild West era where coins were overwhelmingly preferred over paper currency.</li>\r\n<li><span>BRILLIANT UNCIRCULATED CONDITION –</span> Your 1898-P Morgan Annie Oakley Silver Dollar will come in Brilliant Uncirculated (BU) condition.</li>\r\n<li><span>THE CASE OF THE DISAPPEARING MORGANS –</span> While millions of Morgan Silver Dollars were struck from 1878 through 1921, massive silver meltings and the ravages of time have taken their toll. Today coin experts believe that only 15% of all Morgans ever struck remain in existence!</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>Don’t miss your chance to get one of these 1898-P Annie Oakley Morgans. Quantities are extremely limited so click it to your cart right now!</p>'),(3972910,75,1,174503,'<p>The Annie Oakley Silver Dollar</p>\r\n<p>“Little Miss Sure Shot” Annie Oakley may have been only five feet tall, but she was also arguably the deadliest woman of her day with a rifle! Thanks to her incredible marksmanship, Annie joined Buffalo Bill’s touring show in 1885, becoming America’s first female star, performing for royalty across Europe, and earning more than anyone in the company besides Buffalo Bill himself! In 1898, the year this Morgan Silver Dollar was struck, Annie promoted the service of women in combat, going so far as to offer President McKinley the service of 50 female sharpshooters should the U.S. go to war with Spain. The offer wasn’t accepted, but you can still take home this Brilliant Uncirculated (BU) Morgan Silver Dollar struck at the “Mother Mint” in Philadelphia that same year, housed in a custom card featuring Annie Oakley.</p>\r\n<p>COIN HIGHLIGHTS:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>AMERICA’S MOST POPULAR COIN – The Morgan Silver Dollar – so named for its designer, U.S. Mint Assistant Engraver George T. Morgan — has stood the test of time. Struck from 1878-1904 and again in 1921, it was the coin of America’s “Wild West” and jingled in the coin purses of gamblers, gunfighters, soldiers and dance hall girls.</li>\r\n<li>CLASSIC DESIGNS – Morgan’s historic design depicts a profile of Lady Liberty on the obverse while the reverse features an eagle with outstretched wings. The model used for Liberty was Miss Anna Williams of Philadelphia, who Morgan declared to have the most perfect feminine profile he had ever seen.</li>\r\n<li>STRUCK IN GLEAMING AMERICAN SILVER – Struck in 26.73 grams of 90% silver from the famous Comstock Lode, the Morgan Silver Dollar is a big coin 38.1 mm in diameter. When this coin was plunked down on a counter, its weight meant real money, pure and simple.</li>\r\n<li>LEGAL TENDER SILVER DOLLAR – Morgans were $1 legal tender and struck during the heyday of America’s Wild West era where coins were overwhelmingly preferred over paper currency.</li>\r\n<li>BRILLIANT UNCIRCULATED CONDITION – Your 1898-P Morgan Annie Oakley Silver Dollar will come in Brilliant Uncirculated (BU) condition.</li>\r\n<li>THE CASE OF THE DISAPPEARING MORGANS – While millions of Morgan Silver Dollars were struck from 1878 through 1921, massive silver meltings and the ravages of time have taken their toll. Today coin experts believe that only 15% of all Morgans ever struck remain in existence!</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>Don’t miss your chance to get one of these 1898-P Annie Oakley Morgans. Quantities are extremely limited so click it to your cart right now!</p>'),(373150,76,0,174503,'<p><span>“Little Miss Sure Shot” Annie Oakley may have been only five feet tall, but she was also arguably the deadliest woman of her day with a rifle! Thanks to her incredible marksmanship, Annie joined Buffalo Bill’s touring show in 1885, becoming America’s first female star, performing for royalty across Europe, and earning more than anyone in the company besides Buffalo Bill himself!</span></p>'),(3972911,76,1,174503,'<p><span>“Little Miss Sure Shot” Annie Oakley may have been only five feet tall, but she was also arguably the deadliest woman of her day with a rifle! Thanks to her incredible marksmanship, Annie joined Buffalo Bill’s touring show in 1885, becoming America’s first female star, performing for royalty across Europe, and earning more than anyone in the company besides Buffalo Bill himself!</span></p>'),(373151,85,0,174503,'1898-P Morgan Silver Dollar Annie Oakley BU, annie oakley coin, morgan silver dollar, gmrgold, everest.com'),(3972912,85,1,174503,'1898-P Morgan Silver Dollar Annie Oakley BU, annie oakley coin, morgan silver dollar, gmrgold, everest.com'),(373152,75,0,174504,'<p><span>Butch Cassidy and the Sundance Kid were leaders of the \"Wild Bunch,\" which was a posse of rustlers and horse theives. The bandits eventually turned to robbing banks and trains throughout the West in the 1890\'s. Own a Morgan Silver Dollar in Brilliant Uncirculated (BU) condition struck while these desperados were staking out their next heist!</span></p>'),(3972913,75,1,174504,'<p>Butch Cassidy and the Sundance Kid were leaders of the \"Wild Bunch,\" which was a posse of rustlers and horse theives. The bandits eventually turned to robbing banks and trains throughout the West in the 1890\'s. Own a Morgan Silver Dollar in Brilliant Uncirculated (BU) condition struck while these desperados were staking out their next heist!</p>'),(373153,76,0,174504,'<p>Own a Morgan Silver Dollar in Brilliant Uncirculated (BU) condition struck while these desperados were staking out their next heist!</p>'),(3972914,76,1,174504,'<p>Own a Morgan Silver Dollar in Brilliant Uncirculated (BU) condition struck while these desperados were staking out their next heist!</p>'),(373154,85,0,174504,'1896-P Morgan Silver Dollar Butch and Sundance BU, morgan silver dollar, who was butch cassidy and the sundance kid coin, gmrgold, everest.com '),(3972915,85,1,174504,'1896-P Morgan Silver Dollar Butch and Sundance BU, morgan silver dollar, who was butch cassidy and the sundance kid coin, gmrgold, everest.com '),(373155,75,0,174505,'<p><span><span>The King of the Wild Frontier Crowned in Solid Silver</span></span></p>\r\n<p>For millions of Americans eagerly gobbling up stories about their nation’s Wild West Legends, Davy Crockett was indeed the “King of the Wild Frontier” in dozens of dime novels and stage performances. Actor Robert Mayo became typecast as the legendary frontiersman when he played the title role in the 1872 production of <em>Davy Crockett, or Be Sure You\'re Right, Then Go Ahead.</em> The playbills for the performance featured a photograph of the actor decked out as a heavily mustachioed Davy Crockett clad head to toe in buckskin topped off by a rather unique fox skin cap.</p>\r\n<p><span>Classic Image of Davy Crockett</span></p>\r\n<p>Now you can capture that same image thanks to this commemorative round released by the highly respected Intaglio Mint as part of its Wild West Legends series. Struck in a full ounce of highly pure 99.9% fine silver, this silver dollar-sized round features the classic photo of Mayo in full costume below the legend that reads “DAVY CROCKETT” in Western type curved along the circumference. The medal’s reverse shows a logo composed of many iconic Old West images including a sheriff’s badge wrapped with a cowboy’s rope, a horned bull skull, six-shooters and a pair of horseshoes. In addition, the Intaglio Mint One-Ounce Silver Davy Crockett Medals available in this offer come in Gem Brilliant Uncirculated (BU) condition, meaning that each piece is the product of a superb strike that places it firmly among the elite of the run.</p>\r\n<p><span>A Real-Life Legend</span></p>\r\n<p>Despite having many real-life adventures as a frontiersman, explorer, pioneer, folk hero, soldier, and politician, the actual David “Davy” Crockett did not discourage the myths and legends that grew up around him. A three-time congressman from Tennessee, he fought with the Tennessee Militia in the Creek War and later reenlisted to fight in the War of 1812. After being defeated for a seat in Congress in 1835, he famously said, “I told the people of my district that I would serve them as faithfully as I had done; but if not, they might go to hell, and I would go to Texas!” It was there that Crockett died, defending the Alamo in the Texas Revolution against Mexico.</p>\r\n<p>Today, most people — especially those who grew up in the 1950s — envision Davy Crockett as a coonskin cap-wearing hero played by Fess Parker from 1954-1955 on the <em>Walt Disney’s Disneyland</em> television program that featured the song “The Ballad of Davy Crockett.” This artistic one-ounce round is a modern twist on an American legend. Start or add to your collection today with the Intaglio Mint One-Ounce Silver Wild West Legends Davy Crockett Medal. Order yours now!</p>\r\n<p><span>PRODUCT HIGHLIGHTS:</span></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li><span>RUGGED WESTERN DESIGNS –</span> This rugged coin is part of the Intaglio Mint’s Wild West Legends series and features a depiction of Davy Crockett as portrayed by actor Frank Mayo during an 1872 stage production about the famous frontiersman’s life. The medal’s reverse features the series logo that shows a variety of Old West images.</li>\r\n<li><span>STRUCK IN GLEAMING SILVER –</span> Each silver round was struck by the Intaglio Mint in one ounce of highly pure 99.9% fine silver and measures 39 mm in diameter.</li>\r\n<li><span>GEM BRILLIANT UNCIRCULATED CONDITION –</span> Your Intaglio Mint One-Ounce Silver Wild West Legends Davy Crockett Medal comes in Gem Brilliant Uncirculated (BU) condition.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>Celebrate the legend of the “King of the Wild Frontier” with the Intaglio Mint One-Ounce Silver Wild West Legends Davy Crockett Medal. </p>'),(3972916,75,1,174505,'<p>The King of the Wild Frontier Crowned in Solid Silver</p>\r\n<p>For millions of Americans eagerly gobbling up stories about their nation’s Wild West Legends, Davy Crockett was indeed the “King of the Wild Frontier” in dozens of dime novels and stage performances. Actor Robert Mayo became typecast as the legendary frontiersman when he played the title role in the 1872 production of <em>Davy Crockett, or Be Sure You\'re Right, Then Go Ahead.</em> The playbills for the performance featured a photograph of the actor decked out as a heavily mustachioed Davy Crockett clad head to toe in buckskin topped off by a rather unique fox skin cap.</p>\r\n<p>Classic Image of Davy Crockett</p>\r\n<p>Now you can capture that same image thanks to this commemorative round released by the highly respected Intaglio Mint as part of its Wild West Legends series. Struck in a full ounce of highly pure 99.9% fine silver, this silver dollar-sized round features the classic photo of Mayo in full costume below the legend that reads “DAVY CROCKETT” in Western type curved along the circumference. The medal’s reverse shows a logo composed of many iconic Old West images including a sheriff’s badge wrapped with a cowboy’s rope, a horned bull skull, six-shooters and a pair of horseshoes. In addition, the Intaglio Mint One-Ounce Silver Davy Crockett Medals available in this offer come in Gem Brilliant Uncirculated (BU) condition, meaning that each piece is the product of a superb strike that places it firmly among the elite of the run.</p>\r\n<p>A Real-Life Legend</p>\r\n<p>Despite having many real-life adventures as a frontiersman, explorer, pioneer, folk hero, soldier, and politician, the actual David “Davy” Crockett did not discourage the myths and legends that grew up around him. A three-time congressman from Tennessee, he fought with the Tennessee Militia in the Creek War and later reenlisted to fight in the War of 1812. After being defeated for a seat in Congress in 1835, he famously said, “I told the people of my district that I would serve them as faithfully as I had done; but if not, they might go to hell, and I would go to Texas!” It was there that Crockett died, defending the Alamo in the Texas Revolution against Mexico.</p>\r\n<p>Today, most people — especially those who grew up in the 1950s — envision Davy Crockett as a coonskin cap-wearing hero played by Fess Parker from 1954-1955 on the <em>Walt Disney’s Disneyland</em> television program that featured the song “The Ballad of Davy Crockett.” This artistic one-ounce round is a modern twist on an American legend. Start or add to your collection today with the Intaglio Mint One-Ounce Silver Wild West Legends Davy Crockett Medal. Order yours now!</p>\r\n<p>PRODUCT HIGHLIGHTS:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>RUGGED WESTERN DESIGNS – This rugged coin is part of the Intaglio Mint’s Wild West Legends series and features a depiction of Davy Crockett as portrayed by actor Frank Mayo during an 1872 stage production about the famous frontiersman’s life. The medal’s reverse features the series logo that shows a variety of Old West images.</li>\r\n<li>STRUCK IN GLEAMING SILVER – Each silver round was struck by the Intaglio Mint in one ounce of highly pure 99.9% fine silver and measures 39 mm in diameter.</li>\r\n<li>GEM BRILLIANT UNCIRCULATED CONDITION – Your Intaglio Mint One-Ounce Silver Wild West Legends Davy Crockett Medal comes in Gem Brilliant Uncirculated (BU) condition.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>Celebrate the legend of the “King of the Wild Frontier” with the Intaglio Mint One-Ounce Silver Wild West Legends Davy Crockett Medal. </p>'),(373156,76,0,174505,'<p><span>Today, most people — especially those who grew up in the 1950s — envision Davy Crockett as a coonskin cap-wearing hero played by Fess Parker from 1954-1955 on the </span><em>Walt Disney’s Disneyland</em><span> television program that featured the song “The Ballad of Davy Crockett.” This artistic one-ounce round is a modern twist on an American legend. Start or add to your collection today with the Intaglio Mint One-Ounce Silver Wild West Legends Davy Crockett Medal. Order yours now!</span></p>'),(3972917,76,1,174505,'<p><span>Today, most people — especially those who grew up in the 1950s — envision Davy Crockett as a coonskin cap-wearing hero played by Fess Parker from 1954-1955 on the </span><em>Walt Disney’s Disneyland</em><span> television program that featured the song “The Ballad of Davy Crockett.” This artistic one-ounce round is a modern twist on an American legend. Start or add to your collection today with the Intaglio Mint One-Ounce Silver Wild West Legends Davy Crockett Medal. Order yours now!</span></p>'),(373157,85,0,174505,'Intaglio Mint 1-oz Silver Wild West Legends Davy Crockett Medal BU, intaglio mint coins, historical coins, davy crockett, gmrgold, everest.com'),(3972918,85,1,174505,'Intaglio Mint 1-oz Silver Wild West Legends Davy Crockett Medal BU, intaglio mint coins, historical coins, davy crockett, gmrgold, everest.com'),(373158,75,0,174506,'<p><span><span>“I’m Your Huckleberry.\"</span></span></p>\r\n<p>It’s uncertain whether gambler and gunslinger John Henry “Doc” Holliday ever really said that to outlaw Johnny Ringo as depicted in a scene from the classic 1993 film <em>Tombstone</em>, but there’s no questioning that the two were enemies. Forever immortalized for his role as a friend and associate of Wyatt Earp in 1881 at the Gunfight at the OK Corral in Tombstone, Arizona, Holliday was involved in eight known gunfights during his short life and joined Wyatt in his Vendetta Ride to kill those suspected of being involved in the death of Morgan Earp.</p>\r\n<p>This 1887-P Morgan Silver Dollar was struck at the “Mother Mint” in Philadelphia during the last year of Doc Holliday’s short-but-memorable life, a victim of tuberculosis at the age of 36. Plus, each Morgan Dollar available here is in Brilliant Uncirculated (BU) condition and comes housed in a custom card about this Wild West legend.</p>\r\n<p><span><span>COIN HIGHLIGHTS:</span></span></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li><span>AMERICA’S MOST POPULAR COIN –</span> The Morgan Silver Dollar — so named for its designer, U.S. Mint Assistant Engraver George T. Morgan — has stood the test of time. Struck from 1878-1904 and again in 1921, it was the coin of America’s “Wild West” and jingled in the coin purses of gamblers, gunfighters, soldiers and dance hall girls.</li>\r\n<li><span>CLASSIC DESIGNS –</span> Morgan’s historic design depicts a profile of Lady Liberty on the obverse while the reverse features an eagle with outstretched wings. The model used for Liberty was Miss Anna Williams of Philadelphia, who Morgan declared to have the most perfect feminine profile he had ever seen.</li>\r\n<li><span>STRUCK IN GLEAMING AMERICAN SILVER –</span> Struck in 26.73 grams of 90% silver from the famous Comstock Lode, the Morgan Silver Dollar is a big coin measuring 38.1 mm in diameter.</li>\r\n<li><span>LEGAL TENDER SILVER DOLLAR –</span> Morgans were $1 legal tender and struck during the heyday of America’s Wild West era where coins were overwhelmingly preferred over paper currency.</li>\r\n<li><span>BRILLIANT UNCIRCULATED CONDITION –</span> Your 1887-P Morgan Silver Dollar was graded by the Numismatic Guaranty Corporation (NGC) as being in Brilliant Uncirculated (BU) condition.</li>\r\n<li><span>THE CASE OF THE DISAPPEARING MORGANS –</span> While millions of Morgan Silver Dollars were struck from 1878 through 1921, massive silver meltings and the ravages of time have taken their toll. Today coin experts believe that only 15% of all Morgans ever struck remain in existence!</li>\r\n</ul>'),(3972919,75,1,174506,'<p>“I’m Your Huckleberry.\"</p>\r\n<p>It’s uncertain whether gambler and gunslinger John Henry “Doc” Holliday ever really said that to outlaw Johnny Ringo as depicted in a scene from the classic 1993 film <em>Tombstone</em>, but there’s no questioning that the two were enemies. Forever immortalized for his role as a friend and associate of Wyatt Earp in 1881 at the Gunfight at the OK Corral in Tombstone, Arizona, Holliday was involved in eight known gunfights during his short life and joined Wyatt in his Vendetta Ride to kill those suspected of being involved in the death of Morgan Earp.</p>\r\n<p>This 1887-P Morgan Silver Dollar was struck at the “Mother Mint” in Philadelphia during the last year of Doc Holliday’s short-but-memorable life, a victim of tuberculosis at the age of 36. Plus, each Morgan Dollar available here is in Brilliant Uncirculated (BU) condition and comes housed in a custom card about this Wild West legend.</p>\r\n<p>COIN HIGHLIGHTS:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>AMERICA’S MOST POPULAR COIN – The Morgan Silver Dollar — so named for its designer, U.S. Mint Assistant Engraver George T. Morgan — has stood the test of time. Struck from 1878-1904 and again in 1921, it was the coin of America’s “Wild West” and jingled in the coin purses of gamblers, gunfighters, soldiers and dance hall girls.</li>\r\n<li>CLASSIC DESIGNS – Morgan’s historic design depicts a profile of Lady Liberty on the obverse while the reverse features an eagle with outstretched wings. The model used for Liberty was Miss Anna Williams of Philadelphia, who Morgan declared to have the most perfect feminine profile he had ever seen.</li>\r\n<li>STRUCK IN GLEAMING AMERICAN SILVER – Struck in 26.73 grams of 90% silver from the famous Comstock Lode, the Morgan Silver Dollar is a big coin measuring 38.1 mm in diameter.</li>\r\n<li>LEGAL TENDER SILVER DOLLAR – Morgans were $1 legal tender and struck during the heyday of America’s Wild West era where coins were overwhelmingly preferred over paper currency.</li>\r\n<li>BRILLIANT UNCIRCULATED CONDITION – Your 1887-P Morgan Silver Dollar was graded by the Numismatic Guaranty Corporation (NGC) as being in Brilliant Uncirculated (BU) condition.</li>\r\n<li>THE CASE OF THE DISAPPEARING MORGANS – While millions of Morgan Silver Dollars were struck from 1878 through 1921, massive silver meltings and the ravages of time have taken their toll. Today coin experts believe that only 15% of all Morgans ever struck remain in existence!</li>\r\n</ul>'),(373159,76,0,174506,'<p>\"Im Your Huckleberry\"</p>'),(3972920,76,1,174506,'<p>\"Im Your Huckleberry\"</p>'),(373160,85,0,174506,'1887-P Doc Holliday Morgan Silver Dollar BU, Doc holliday memorabilia, who was doc holliday?, gmrgold coins, doc holliday coins, everest.com '),(3972921,85,1,174506,'1887-P Doc Holliday Morgan Silver Dollar BU, Doc holliday memorabilia, who was doc holliday?, gmrgold coins, doc holliday coins, everest.com '),(373161,75,0,174507,'<p><span><span>Who Killed Johnny Ringo?</span></span></p>\r\n<p>Johnny Ringo was a Shakespeare-quoting gunslinger whose wit was as quick as his gun. Soon after settling in Tombstone, Arizona, he aligned himself with the outlaw faction that faced Wyatt Earp. Though he did not take part in the famous gunfight at the OK Corral, his body was found in 1882 lying against a tree in West Turkey Creek Valley with a bullet hole in his head, his horse two miles away with his boots still tied to the saddle. Among the people credited with his killing include Frank Leslie, Michael “Johnny-Behind-the-Deuce,” O’Rourke, Wyatt Earp and Doc Holliday. In truth no one’s sure just who killed Ringo. With no evidence to point to a guilty party the coroner’s inquest officially ruled his death a suicide.</p>\r\n<p>This 1882-O Morgan Silver Dollar was struck at the New Orleans Mint the same year Johnny Ringo was found dead, his death still an unsolved mystery. Plus, each Morgan Dollar available here is in Brilliant Uncirculated (BU) condition and comes housed in a custom card about this Wild West legend.</p>\r\n<p><span><span>COIN HIGHLIGHTS:</span></span></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li><span>AMERICA’S MOST POPULAR COIN –</span> The Morgan Silver Dollar — so named for its designer, U.S. Mint Assistant Engraver George T. Morgan — has stood the test of time. Struck from 1878-1904 and again in 1921, it was the coin of America’s “Wild West” and jingled in the coin purses of gamblers, gunfighters, soldiers and dance hall girls.</li>\r\n<li><span>CLASSIC DESIGNS –</span> Morgan’s historic design depicts a profile of Lady Liberty on the obverse while the reverse features an eagle with outstretched wings. The model used for Liberty was Miss Anna Williams of Philadelphia, who Morgan declared to have the most perfect feminine profile he had ever seen.</li>\r\n<li><span>STRUCK IN GLEAMING AMERICAN SILVER –</span> Struck in 26.73 grams of 90% silver from the famous Comstock Lode, the Morgan Silver Dollar is a big coin measuring 38.1 mm in diameter.</li>\r\n<li><span>LEGAL TENDER SILVER DOLLAR –</span> Morgans were $1 legal tender and struck during the heyday of America’s Wild West era where coins were overwhelmingly preferred over paper currency.</li>\r\n<li><span>BRILLIANT UNCIRCULATED CONDITION –</span> Your 1882-O Morgan Silver Dollar was graded by the Numismatic Guaranty Corporation (NGC) as being in Brilliant Uncirculated (BU) condition.</li>\r\n<li><span>THE CASE OF THE DISAPPEARING MORGANS –</span> While millions of Morgan Silver Dollars were struck from 1878 through 1921, massive silver meltings and the ravages of time have taken their toll. Today coin experts believe that only 15% of all Morgans ever struck remain in existence!</li>\r\n</ul>'),(3972922,75,1,174507,'<p>Who Killed Johnny Ringo?</p>\r\n<p>Johnny Ringo was a Shakespeare-quoting gunslinger whose wit was as quick as his gun. Soon after settling in Tombstone, Arizona, he aligned himself with the outlaw faction that faced Wyatt Earp. Though he did not take part in the famous gunfight at the OK Corral, his body was found in 1882 lying against a tree in West Turkey Creek Valley with a bullet hole in his head, his horse two miles away with his boots still tied to the saddle. Among the people credited with his killing include Frank Leslie, Michael “Johnny-Behind-the-Deuce,” O’Rourke, Wyatt Earp and Doc Holliday. In truth no one’s sure just who killed Ringo. With no evidence to point to a guilty party the coroner’s inquest officially ruled his death a suicide.</p>\r\n<p>This 1882-O Morgan Silver Dollar was struck at the New Orleans Mint the same year Johnny Ringo was found dead, his death still an unsolved mystery. Plus, each Morgan Dollar available here is in Brilliant Uncirculated (BU) condition and comes housed in a custom card about this Wild West legend.</p>\r\n<p>COIN HIGHLIGHTS:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>AMERICA’S MOST POPULAR COIN – The Morgan Silver Dollar — so named for its designer, U.S. Mint Assistant Engraver George T. Morgan — has stood the test of time. Struck from 1878-1904 and again in 1921, it was the coin of America’s “Wild West” and jingled in the coin purses of gamblers, gunfighters, soldiers and dance hall girls.</li>\r\n<li>CLASSIC DESIGNS – Morgan’s historic design depicts a profile of Lady Liberty on the obverse while the reverse features an eagle with outstretched wings. The model used for Liberty was Miss Anna Williams of Philadelphia, who Morgan declared to have the most perfect feminine profile he had ever seen.</li>\r\n<li>STRUCK IN GLEAMING AMERICAN SILVER – Struck in 26.73 grams of 90% silver from the famous Comstock Lode, the Morgan Silver Dollar is a big coin measuring 38.1 mm in diameter.</li>\r\n<li>LEGAL TENDER SILVER DOLLAR – Morgans were $1 legal tender and struck during the heyday of America’s Wild West era where coins were overwhelmingly preferred over paper currency.</li>\r\n<li>BRILLIANT UNCIRCULATED CONDITION – Your 1882-O Morgan Silver Dollar was graded by the Numismatic Guaranty Corporation (NGC) as being in Brilliant Uncirculated (BU) condition.</li>\r\n<li>THE CASE OF THE DISAPPEARING MORGANS – While millions of Morgan Silver Dollars were struck from 1878 through 1921, massive silver meltings and the ravages of time have taken their toll. Today coin experts believe that only 15% of all Morgans ever struck remain in existence!</li>\r\n</ul>'),(373162,76,0,174507,'<p><span>Get a piece of America’s Wild West with this 1882-O New Orleans Mint Morgan in gorgeous Brilliant Uncirculated condition!</span></p>'),(3972923,76,1,174507,'<p><span>Get a piece of America’s Wild West with this 1882-O New Orleans Mint Morgan in gorgeous Brilliant Uncirculated condition!</span></p>'),(373163,85,0,174507,'1882-O Johnny Ringo Morgan Silver Dollar BU, who killed johnny ringo?, who was johnny ringo?, what is BU?, morgan silver dollar, gmrgold, everest.com'),(3972924,85,1,174507,'1882-O Johnny Ringo Morgan Silver Dollar BU, who killed johnny ringo?, who was johnny ringo?, what is BU?, morgan silver dollar, gmrgold, everest.com'),(373167,75,0,174509,'<p><span><span>The Emblem of the Old West’s Most Famous Lawmen</span></span></p>\r\n<p>Among the finest lawmen ever to track down outlaws and renegades in the Old West were the Texas Rangers. Described as the “men who could not be stampeded,” the Rangers have a history dating back to the earliest settlements in Texas. Often outnumbered, outgunned and underpaid, the Rangers down through the years have drawn comparisons to the FBI, Scotland Yard, and the Royal Canadian Mounted Police. To have worn the star of the Texas Rangers stood for something, and now it can stand for something in your collection thanks to this spectacular silver round!</p>\r\n<p><span>The Badge of the Texas Rangers Rides Again</span></p>\r\n<p>Struck by the Intaglio Mint in two ounces of highly pure 99.9% silver, this collectible round pays tribute to the fabled Texas Rangers by featuring their famous five-pointed star badge — a badge that struck fear into the hearts of owl hoots, gunslingers and bandits throughout Texas during the 1800s. In the center of the star is, the inscription “CO. A,” which stands for Company A, one of six Rangers companies. Company A encompasses 35 counties within an area bounded by the State of Louisiana and the Texas Gulf Coast. Along the top and bottom of the round are the words TEXAS RANGERS. The star, set within the circle of the round, resembles a wagon wheel and within each space between the spokes one can see the round’s silver weight and purity. The round’s reverse design features a stylized image of an eagle killing a snake as seen on Mexican Pesos.</p>\r\n<p>Each Intaglio Mint Two-Ounce Silver Texas Rangers Round also comes with a blazing antiqued finish that makes it appear as if it has just stepped out of the pages of Wild West history. The darkened and shaded images perfectly with the round’s razor-sharp details to create a piece you’ll be proud to pin into your collection. Here’s your chance to step back in time to an era when the law was represented by tough men and fast guns. Order yours today!</p>\r\n<p><span><span>PRODUCT HIGHLIGHTS:</span></span></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li><span>A BADGE OF HONOR –</span> This collectible round pays tribute to the life, legend and deeds of the famous Texas Ranges. It features a design of a star-shaped badge on one side and on the other a stylized image of an eagle killing a snake as seen on Mexican Pesos.</li>\r\n<li><span>STRUCK IN HIGHLY PURE SILVER –</span> Each Silver Texas Rangers Badge Round was struck in two ounces of highly pure 99.9% silver and measures 39 mm in diameter.</li>\r\n<li><span>BLAZING ANTIQUED FINISH –</span> Your Intaglio Mint Two-Ounce Silver Texas Rangers Badge Round comes with a blazing antiqued finish as if it stepped out of the pages of the Old West.</li>\r\n</ul>'),(3972925,75,1,174509,'<p>The Emblem of the Old West’s Most Famous Lawmen</p>\r\n<p>Among the finest lawmen ever to track down outlaws and renegades in the Old West were the Texas Rangers. Described as the “men who could not be stampeded,” the Rangers have a history dating back to the earliest settlements in Texas. Often outnumbered, outgunned and underpaid, the Rangers down through the years have drawn comparisons to the FBI, Scotland Yard, and the Royal Canadian Mounted Police. To have worn the star of the Texas Rangers stood for something, and now it can stand for something in your collection thanks to this spectacular silver round!</p>\r\n<p>The Badge of the Texas Rangers Rides Again</p>\r\n<p>Struck by the Intaglio Mint in two ounces of highly pure 99.9% silver, this collectible round pays tribute to the fabled Texas Rangers by featuring their famous five-pointed star badge — a badge that struck fear into the hearts of owl hoots, gunslingers and bandits throughout Texas during the 1800s. In the center of the star is, the inscription “CO. A,” which stands for Company A, one of six Rangers companies. Company A encompasses 35 counties within an area bounded by the State of Louisiana and the Texas Gulf Coast. Along the top and bottom of the round are the words TEXAS RANGERS. The star, set within the circle of the round, resembles a wagon wheel and within each space between the spokes one can see the round’s silver weight and purity. The round’s reverse design features a stylized image of an eagle killing a snake as seen on Mexican Pesos.</p>\r\n<p>Each Intaglio Mint Two-Ounce Silver Texas Rangers Round also comes with a blazing antiqued finish that makes it appear as if it has just stepped out of the pages of Wild West history. The darkened and shaded images perfectly with the round’s razor-sharp details to create a piece you’ll be proud to pin into your collection. Here’s your chance to step back in time to an era when the law was represented by tough men and fast guns. Order yours today!</p>\r\n<p>PRODUCT HIGHLIGHTS:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>A BADGE OF HONOR – This collectible round pays tribute to the life, legend and deeds of the famous Texas Ranges. It features a design of a star-shaped badge on one side and on the other a stylized image of an eagle killing a snake as seen on Mexican Pesos.</li>\r\n<li>STRUCK IN HIGHLY PURE SILVER – Each Silver Texas Rangers Badge Round was struck in two ounces of highly pure 99.9% silver and measures 39 mm in diameter.</li>\r\n<li>BLAZING ANTIQUED FINISH – Your Intaglio Mint Two-Ounce Silver Texas Rangers Badge Round comes with a blazing antiqued finish as if it stepped out of the pages of the Old West.</li>\r\n</ul>'),(373168,76,0,174509,'<p>The Badge of the Texas Rangers Rides Again</p>\r\n<p>2 ounce silver</p>'),(3972926,76,1,174509,'<p>The Badge of the Texas Rangers Rides Again</p>\r\n<p>2 ounce silver</p>'),(373169,85,0,174509,'Intaglio Mint 2-oz Silver Texas Rangers Badge Round Antiqued, 2 ounce silver, texas rangers badge, gmrgold, everest.com'),(3972927,85,1,174509,'Intaglio Mint 2-oz Silver Texas Rangers Badge Round Antiqued, 2 ounce silver, texas rangers badge, gmrgold, everest.com'),(373170,75,0,174510,'<p><span>Werewolves Beware!</span></p>\r\n<p>There are many ways to add shining 99.9% fine silver to your collection, but there’s only one way to do it that will make the local werewolves stay in line – silver bullets! Now you can add some real firepower to your silver stacks with this non-firing collectible modeled after the .45 caliber bullets used in the Automatic Colt Pistol (ACP). The semi-automatic pistol was a standard issue sidearm for United States Armed Forces from 1911 to 1986 and saw action in World War I, World War II, the Korean War and the Vietnam War, making these bullets about as American as you can get!</p>\r\n<p>Minted in one full ounce of highly pure 99.9% silver, each .45 Caliber Pistol Round has been carefully struck to mimic the stunning appearance of fresh steel-cased bullets. Just one look at these bullets and you can get a sense of realism that conveys a simple message: This baby means business! </p>\r\n<p>This non-firing One-Ounce Silver Bullet .45 Caliber Pistol Round Replica is fun way for anyone looking to add some silver to their collection to load up. It’s also the perfect gift for any firearm (or werewolf) enthusiast you know. </p>'),(373503,75,1,174510,'<p><span>Werewolves Beware!</span></p>\r\n<p>There are many ways to add shining 99.9% fine silver to your collection, but there’s only one way to do it that will make the local werewolves stay in line – silver bullets! Now you can add some real firepower to your silver stacks with this non-firing collectible modeled after the .45 caliber bullets used in the Automatic Colt Pistol (ACP). The semi-automatic pistol was a standard issue sidearm for United States Armed Forces from 1911 to 1986 and saw action in World War I, World War II, the Korean War and the Vietnam War, making these bullets about as American as you can get!</p>\r\n<p>Minted in one full ounce of highly pure 99.9% silver, each .45 Caliber Pistol Round has been carefully struck to mimic the stunning appearance of fresh steel-cased bullets. Just one look at these bullets and you can get a sense of realism that conveys a simple message: This baby means business! </p>\r\n<p>This non-firing One-Ounce Silver Bullet .45 Caliber Pistol Round Replica is fun way for anyone looking to add some silver to their collection to load up. It’s also the perfect gift for any firearm (or werewolf) enthusiast you know. </p>'),(373171,76,0,174510,'<div class=\"page-title-wrapper product\">\r\n<p class=\"page-title\"><span class=\"base\" data-ui-id=\"page-title-wrapper\">1-oz Silver Bullet – .45 Caliber Pistol Round Replica</span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"page messages\">\r\n<div data-placeholder=\"messages\"></div>\r\n<div data-bind=\"scope: \'messages\'\"></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div></div>\r\n<div class=\"columns\">\r\n<div class=\"column main row clear-after\">\r\n<div class=\"block block-compare\" data-bind=\"scope: \'compareProducts\'\" data-role=\"compare-products-sidebar\"></div>\r\n<div class=\"col-xs-12 col-sm-8 col-lg-8 product media product-view-image-container\"><a id=\"gallery-prev-area\" tabindex=\"-1\"></a>\r\n<div class=\"action-skip-wrapper\"></div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>'),(373504,76,1,174510,'<div class=\"page-title-wrapper product\">\r\n<p class=\"page-title\"><span class=\"base\" data-ui-id=\"page-title-wrapper\">1-oz Silver Bullet – .45 Caliber Pistol Round Replica</span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"page messages\">\r\n<div data-placeholder=\"messages\"></div>\r\n<div data-bind=\"scope: \'messages\'\"></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div></div>\r\n<div class=\"columns\">\r\n<div class=\"column main row clear-after\">\r\n<div class=\"block block-compare\" data-bind=\"scope: \'compareProducts\'\" data-role=\"compare-products-sidebar\"></div>\r\n<div class=\"col-xs-12 col-sm-8 col-lg-8 product media product-view-image-container\"><a id=\"gallery-prev-area\" tabindex=\"-1\"></a>\r\n<div class=\"action-skip-wrapper\"></div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>'),(373172,85,0,174510,'1-oz Silver Bullet – .45 Caliber Pistol Round Replica, silver bullet, 1 ounce silver bullet, 1oz silver bullet, 45 acp silver bullet, gmrgold.com, everest\r\n'),(373505,85,1,174510,'1-oz Silver Bullet – .45 Caliber Pistol Round Replica, silver bullet, 1 ounce silver bullet, 1oz silver bullet, 45 acp silver bullet, gmrgold.com, everest\r\n'),(373173,75,0,174511,'<p>The 1901-O \"Teddy Roosevelt\" Silver Dollar</p>\r\n<p>The contribution President Theodore Roosevelt made to U.S. coinage is immeasurable. While he\'s famous for commissioning new Saint - Gaudens gold coin designs, the 1901 New Orleans Morgan Silver Dollar was actually the first U.S. coin struck during his presidency. It was right at the end of the first mintage of Morgan Silver Dollars, and can be very hard to find today in the Brilliant Uncirculated condition you get here. It\'s a beaut! Each comes in a custom 4\" by 6\" display case. Get yours now!</p>'),(3972928,75,1,174511,'<p>The 1901-O \"Teddy Roosevelt\" Silver Dollar</p>\r\n<p>The contribution President Theodore Roosevelt made to U.S. coinage is immeasurable. While he\'s famous for commissioning new Saint - Gaudens gold coin designs, the 1901 New Orleans Morgan Silver Dollar was actually the first U.S. coin struck during his presidency. It was right at the end of the first mintage of Morgan Silver Dollars, and can be very hard to find today in the Brilliant Uncirculated condition you get here. It\'s a beaut! Each comes in a custom 4\" by 6\" display case. Get yours now!</p>'),(373174,76,0,174511,'<p>The 1901-O \"Teddy Roosevelt\" Silver Dollar</p>'),(3972929,76,1,174511,'<p>The 1901-O \"Teddy Roosevelt\" Silver Dollar</p>'),(373175,85,0,174511,'1901-O Morgan Silver Dollar \"Teddy Roosevelt\" BU, father of conservation, teddy roosevelt, president roosevelt coin, gmrgold, everest.com\r\n'),(3972930,85,1,174511,'1901-O Morgan Silver Dollar \"Teddy Roosevelt\" BU, father of conservation, teddy roosevelt, president roosevelt coin, gmrgold, everest.com\r\n'),(373176,75,0,174512,'<p><span><span>Capture the Legend of the Wild West’s Most Famous Lawman</span></span></p>\r\n<p>Wyatt Earp has been portrayed on film by such Hollywood heavyweights as Randolph Scott, Henry Fonda, Burt Lancaster, Kurt Russell and Kevin Costner, each capturing the quiet and commanding presence of the fearless lawman in his own way. And now one of the most famous figures of the Wild West is being portrayed on a nicely detailed silver round that captures his grim visage all the way down to his unforgettable handlebar mustache.</p>\r\n<p><span>Silver Medal Lets You Come Face to Face With Wyatt Earp</span></p>\r\n<p>Based on a famous photograph taken of Wyatt Earp in 1887, this commemorative round was released by the highly respected Intaglio Mint as part of its Wild West Legends series. Struck in a full ounce of highly pure 99.9% fine silver, this silver dollar-sized round features a portrait of a gaunt Wyatt Earp with searing eyes below a legend that reads “WYATT EARP” in Western type curved along the circumference. The medal’s reverse shows a logo composed of many iconic Old West images including a sheriff’s badge wrapped with a cowboy’s rope, a horned bull skull, six-shooters and a pair of horseshoes. In addition, the Intaglio Mint One-Ounce Silver Wyatt Earp Medals available in this offer come in Gem Brilliant Uncirculated (BU) condition, meaning that each piece is the product of a superb strike that places it firmly among the elite of the run.</p>\r\n<p>Though he is most famous for his role in the Gunfight at the OK Corral in Tombstone, Arizona, Wyatt Earp was also a saloonkeeper, gambler, gunslinger and confidence man. Prior to coming to Tombstone, he had worked as an assistant marshal in Dodge City, Kansas, a booming center of the cattle trade that was hailed as the “Wickedest Little City in the West.” Earp was the last surviving participant in the OK Corral gunfight, passing away in 1929 at the age of 80 at his home in Los Angeles</p>\r\n<p>This artistic one-ounce round is a modern twist on an American legend. Start or add to your collection today with the Intaglio Mint One-Ounce Silver Wild West Legends Wyatt Earp Medal. Order yours now!</p>\r\n<p><span>COIN HIGHLIGHTS:</span></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li><span>RUGGED WESTERN DESIGNS –</span> This rugged coin is part of the Intaglio Mint’s Wild West Legends series and features a depiction of Wyatt Earp. The medal’s reverse features the series logo that shows a variety of Old West images.</li>\r\n<li><span>STRUCK IN GLEAMING SILVER –</span> Each silver round was struck by the Intaglio Mint in one ounce of highly pure 99.9% fine silver and measures 39 mm in diameter.</li>\r\n<li><span>GEM BRILLIANT UNCIRCULATED CONDITION –</span> Your Intaglio Mint One-Ounce Silver Wild West Legends Wyatt Earp Medal comes in Gem Brilliant Uncirculated (BU) condition.</li>\r\n</ul>'),(3972931,75,1,174512,'<p>Capture the Legend of the Wild West’s Most Famous Lawman</p>\r\n<p>Wyatt Earp has been portrayed on film by such Hollywood heavyweights as Randolph Scott, Henry Fonda, Burt Lancaster, Kurt Russell and Kevin Costner, each capturing the quiet and commanding presence of the fearless lawman in his own way. And now one of the most famous figures of the Wild West is being portrayed on a nicely detailed silver round that captures his grim visage all the way down to his unforgettable handlebar mustache.</p>\r\n<p>Silver Medal Lets You Come Face to Face With Wyatt Earp</p>\r\n<p>Based on a famous photograph taken of Wyatt Earp in 1887, this commemorative round was released by the highly respected Intaglio Mint as part of its Wild West Legends series. Struck in a full ounce of highly pure 99.9% fine silver, this silver dollar-sized round features a portrait of a gaunt Wyatt Earp with searing eyes below a legend that reads “WYATT EARP” in Western type curved along the circumference. The medal’s reverse shows a logo composed of many iconic Old West images including a sheriff’s badge wrapped with a cowboy’s rope, a horned bull skull, six-shooters and a pair of horseshoes. In addition, the Intaglio Mint One-Ounce Silver Wyatt Earp Medals available in this offer come in Gem Brilliant Uncirculated (BU) condition, meaning that each piece is the product of a superb strike that places it firmly among the elite of the run.</p>\r\n<p>Though he is most famous for his role in the Gunfight at the OK Corral in Tombstone, Arizona, Wyatt Earp was also a saloonkeeper, gambler, gunslinger and confidence man. Prior to coming to Tombstone, he had worked as an assistant marshal in Dodge City, Kansas, a booming center of the cattle trade that was hailed as the “Wickedest Little City in the West.” Earp was the last surviving participant in the OK Corral gunfight, passing away in 1929 at the age of 80 at his home in Los Angeles</p>\r\n<p>This artistic one-ounce round is a modern twist on an American legend. Start or add to your collection today with the Intaglio Mint One-Ounce Silver Wild West Legends Wyatt Earp Medal. Order yours now!</p>\r\n<p>COIN HIGHLIGHTS:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>RUGGED WESTERN DESIGNS – This rugged coin is part of the Intaglio Mint’s Wild West Legends series and features a depiction of Wyatt Earp. The medal’s reverse features the series logo that shows a variety of Old West images.</li>\r\n<li>STRUCK IN GLEAMING SILVER – Each silver round was struck by the Intaglio Mint in one ounce of highly pure 99.9% fine silver and measures 39 mm in diameter.</li>\r\n<li>GEM BRILLIANT UNCIRCULATED CONDITION – Your Intaglio Mint One-Ounce Silver Wild West Legends Wyatt Earp Medal comes in Gem Brilliant Uncirculated (BU) condition.</li>\r\n</ul>'),(373177,76,0,174512,'<p><br class=\"Apple-interchange-newline\" />Based on a famous photograph taken of Wyatt Earp in 1887, this commemorative round was released by the highly respected Intaglio Mint as part of its Wild West Legends series.</p>'),(3972932,76,1,174512,'<p><br class=\"Apple-interchange-newline\" />Based on a famous photograph taken of Wyatt Earp in 1887, this commemorative round was released by the highly respected Intaglio Mint as part of its Wild West Legends series.</p>'),(373178,85,0,174512,'Intaglio Mint 1-oz Silver Wild West Legends Wyatt Earp Medal BU, wyatt earp coin, intaglio mint coins, gmrgold, everest.com'),(3972933,85,1,174512,'Intaglio Mint 1-oz Silver Wild West Legends Wyatt Earp Medal BU, wyatt earp coin, intaglio mint coins, gmrgold, everest.com'),(373179,75,0,174513,'<p><span>Fortify your investment position by collecting Gold, Silver, Platinum, and Copper for your portfolio. Enjoy a one month distinguished bullion box without having to subscribe. The distinguished bullion box is the best box available through BBS. It may contain: silver, gold, platinum in various bars, rounds or coins.</span></p>'),(373180,76,0,174513,'<ul>\r\n<li>The Distinguished Bullion Box by Bullion Box </li>\r\n<li>Silver</li>\r\n<li>Gold</li>\r\n<li>Platinum</li>\r\n</ul>'),(669903,76,1,174513,'<ul>\r\n<li>The Distinguished Bullion Box by Bullion Box </li>\r\n<li>Silver</li>\r\n<li>Gold</li>\r\n<li>Platinum</li>\r\n</ul>'),(373181,85,0,174513,'bullion box, bullion subscription, bullion box subscription, monthly precious metals, precious metals subscription, subscription for precious metals, everest.com'),(373182,75,0,174514,'<h3><strong>6 HD Lens RX-Able Shooting Glass Kit</strong></h3>\r\n<h3>For all shooting disciplines, the Methow Kit from SSP Eyewear provides the most versatile safety shooting glass kit available.  Trap, Skeet, Sporting Clay, and 5 stand, look no further, this is the best solution on the market.</h3>\r\n<p>With optional <strong><span>Methow RX Adapter</span> </strong> for people who wear prescription glasses. Packaged with 6 different colored anti-fog lenses for any light condition. </p>\r\n<p>To prevent blind spots, we created a clear adjustable full-floating nose-piece. Fits numerous face and nose shapes while providing an incredibly comfortable fit. You will forget you are even wearing these glasses. <span><strong>Always take time to adjust the nose bridge for optimal viewing.  This is critical to match the glasses and insert to your particular nose and face shape.</strong></span></p>\r\n<p><strong>Kit includes 2 clear and 1 black adjustable nose pad, padded zippered hard case, cleaning cloth, lanyard and lens changing directions.</strong></p>\r\n<p><b>Designed for:</b></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>All shooting disciplines, particularly those who enjoy trap shooting, skeet, and sporting clays</li>\r\n<li>Hunters</li>\r\n<li>Archers</li>\r\n<li>Mountain bikers</li>\r\n<li>Outdoor enthusiasts </li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p><b>Features:</b></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li><span>Sleek lightweight UV resistant TR90 nylon matte black f</span>rame eliminates glare</li>\r\n<li>Accepts TR90 RX clear adapter for prescriptions <strong><span>(Sold Separately Here)</span></strong></li>\r\n<li>1-piece polycarbonate <span>wrap-around lenses offer full coverage and all are 100% UVA and UVB rated</span></li>\r\n<li>Semi-Rimless frame</li>\r\n<li>Adjustable full-floating clear nose bridge for unbelievable comfort</li>\r\n<li>Double Injected Rubber temples keeps glasses in place</li>\r\n<li>2 Adjustable nose pads clear and black</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<li><strong>Kit Includes:</strong></li>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Six <strong>permanent anti-fog lenses</strong> in clear, yellow, orange, purple, pink and bronze</li>\r\n<li>Nylon matte black f<span>rame</span></li>\r\n<li>Microfiber cleaning cloth</li>\r\n<li>Hard zippered storage case with foam lens separators</li>\r\n<li>Black foam Eyewear retainer</li>\r\n<li>Paper instructions for changing lenses</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</ul>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li><strong>Compliance: </strong></li>\r\n<li><strong></strong>Exceeds ANSI Z87.1+2015 standa